{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019kf2iGJgxy5YdshcYgMdPf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Experiment Plan — policy_ambiguity_safety\n2\t# Post-MVP, targeting EMNLP 2026 (ARR Aug cycle)\n3\t# Claims reference paper_framing.md\n4\t\n5\texperiments:\n6\t  # === P0: Must-run for paper ===\n7\t\n8\t  - id: plan_001\n9\t    name: full_study_clause_generation\n10\t    claim: \"C1, C2, C3\"\n11\t    description: >\n12\t      Generate remaining clauses for full study: coreferential (50 new),\n13\t      authorization_scope (50 new), lexical (+20 to reach 50),\n14\t      incompleteness (+20 to reach 50). Total 140 new clauses.\n15\t      Validate all 300 clauses (50/type × 6 types) for completeness\n16\t      and cross-type balance. Mix CP format per Reviewer suggestion\n17\t      (labeled + unlabeled).\n18\t    priority: P0\n19\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n20\t    deps: []\n21\t    status: planned\n22\t\n23\t  - id: plan_001b\n24\t    name: new_type_mini_pilot\n25\t    claim: \"C1 (validation)\"\n26\t    description: >\n27\t      Mini-pilot for coreferential + authorization_scope (never tested):\n28\t      5 clauses/type × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes.\n29\t      Verify: (a) ambiguous triggers violations (b) unambiguous control < 15%.\n30\t      If systematic issues found, fix clause design before full study.\n31\t      API cost negligible (~$2). Per Reviewer warning on untested types.\n32\t    priority: P0\n33\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n34\t    deps: [plan_001]\n35\t    status: planned\n36\t\n37\t  - id: plan_002\n38\t    name: full_study_api\n39\t    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4, C5\"\n40\t    description: >\n41\t      Run 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1,\n42\t      claude-sonnet-4-6) = 1,800 episodes on τ²-bench. Cross-judge\n43\t      evaluation. Output: episodes.jsonl + judgments.jsonl. No GPU needed.\n44\t      Claude via OpenRouter proxy (base_url=http://47.94.22.126/v1).\n45\t      [2026-05-20] Claude added per distill gap (4/8 papers use Claude baseline).\n46\t    priority: P0\n47\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n48\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_001b, plan_010]\n49\t    status: planned\n50\t\n51\t  - id: plan_003\n52\t    name: full_study_opensource\n53\t    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4, C5\"\n54\t    description: >\n55\t      Run 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models via OpenRouter API:\n56\t      qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b (235B MoE, Alibaba) + deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324\n57\t      (DeepSeek) = 1,200 episodes on τ²-bench. Cross-judge uses API models.\n58\t      Can run in parallel with plan_002. No GPU needed.\n59\t      [2026-05-20] Pivoted from local GPU → API: OpenRouter proxy confirmed\n60\t      to support Qwen3 and DeepSeek models. Eliminates 48h GPU requirement.\n61\t      Provider prefix required (e.g. qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b, not qwen3-235b-a22b).\n62\t    priority: P0\n63\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n64\t    deps: [plan_001]\n65\t    status: planned\n66\t\n67\t  - id: plan_004\n68\t    name: full_study_analysis\n69\t    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4\"\n70\t    description: >\n71\t      Statistical analysis of full study data (3,000 episodes):\n72\t      (a) Binary effect per type with bootstrap CI (C1)\n73\t      (b) Omnibus χ² + pairwise across 6 types (C2)\n74\t      (c) Visibility comparison: CP vs scopal rates (C3)\n75\t      (d) Model × type interaction: 5×6 contingency + logistic regression (C4)\n76\t      Report effect sizes + CI for all comparisons per Reviewer suggestion.\n77\t      [Dream A3] Power analysis: report MDE for C2 (given N=250/type pooled)\n78\t      and C3 (given N=250 per type). If V < 0.20 but MDE > observed V,\n79\t      discuss underpowered possibility.\n80\t      [Dream A4] TOST equivalence test with both ±15pp and ±10pp margins.\n81\t      Justify margin choice explicitly.\n82\t      [Dream A10] Report per-type information delta (token count difference\n83\t      between ambiguous and unambiguous variants) as control variable.\n84\t      [Dream B&K] Inter-model agreement on ambiguous clauses: do 5 models\n85\t      adopt same or different interpretations? (supplementary analysis)\n86\t    priority: P0\n87\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n88\t    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n89\t    status: planned\n90\t\n91\t  - id: plan_005\n92\t    name: error_analysis\n93\t    claim: \"C5\"\n94\t    description: >\n95\t      Qualitative analysis of agent traces from full study:\n96\t      (a) Sample 50 violation traces per type (300 total)\n97\t      (b) Classify failure modes (scope misapplication, conservative refusal,\n98\t          assumption-based action, arbitrary rule selection, etc.)\n99\t      (c) Cross-type failure mode distribution\n100\t      (d) Visibility mechanism: compare CP traces (explicit conflict detection\n101\t          behavior) vs scopal traces (surface scope adoption without awareness)\n102\t      (e) Model-specific failure patterns (connect to C4)\n103\t    priority: P0\n104\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n105\t    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n106\t    status: planned\n107\t\n108\t  # === P1: Important for robustness ===\n109\t\n110\t  - id: plan_006\n111\t    name: reliability_test\n112\t    claim: \"C1, C2\"\n113\t    description: >\n114\t      Test-retest reliability: select 30 representative clauses (5/type),\n115\t      run 3 independent replicates × 2 conditions × 2 API models (gpt-5.4,\n116\t      gpt-4.1) = 360 episodes. Local models added when plan_003 GPU available.\n117\t      Compute ICC for per-clause violation rates. Addresses Reviewer warning\n118\t      about ±8pp sampling noise (scopal 51.7% → 43.3% across MVP/diag).\n119\t      Bootstrap CI width should be < 10pp for key comparisons.\n120\t      [2026-05-20] API portion: 330/360 episodes complete (28/30 clauses),\n121\t      judgments pending.\n122\t    priority: P1\n123\t    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n124\t    deps: [plan_001]\n125\t    status: planned\n126\t\n127\t  - id: plan_007\n128\t    name: realism_validation\n129\t    claim: \"C1 (methodological)\"\n130\t    description: >\n131\t      Validate synthetic ambiguity injection realism:\n132\t      (a) Linguistic property comparison with DRIP-R natural ambiguities\n133\t          (sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR) + KS tests\n134\t      (b) Optional: discriminator test if DRIP-R data accessible\n135\t      Addresses RC4 (ecological validity).\n136\t    priority: P1\n137\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n138\t    deps: [plan_001]\n139\t    status: planned\n140\t\n141\t  - id: plan_009\n142\t    name: judge_calibration\n143\t    claim: \"C1 (methodological)\"\n144\t    description: >\n145\t      LLM-as-judge calibration per distilled research norm (5/8 papers):\n146\t      (a) Sample 100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition\n147\t      (b) Human expert labels (2 annotators, target κ ≥ 0.75)\n148\t      (c) Compute judge precision/recall/F1 against human ground truth\n149\t      (d) Per-severity-tier agreement rates\n150\t      (e) Report in Method section as standard practice per AgentAuditor/DRIP-R\n151\t      [Dream A7] Upgraded P1→P0: Dream best-tier reviewers identified this\n152\t      as \"single most critical missing validation.\" Without it, entire\n153\t      measurement chain from episode to violation label is unvalidated.\n154\t      κ=0.91 measures LLM-LLM agreement, not accuracy.\n155\t    priority: P0\n156\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n157\t    deps: [plan_002]\n158\t    status: planned\n159\t\n160\t  - id: plan_010\n161\t    name: perturbation_control\n162\t    claim: \"C1 (causal validity)\"\n163\t    description: >\n164\t      [Dream A9] Non-ambiguity perturbation control arm to distinguish\n165\t      ambiguity-specific harm from general prompt brittleness.\n166\t      Generate 30 clause pairs with non-ambiguity perturbations:\n167\t      (a) 15 synonym substitution pairs (replace key terms with synonyms)\n168\t      (b) 15 clause reordering pairs (reorder conditions without changing meaning)\n169\t      Run 30 × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6) = 180 episodes.\n170\t      Key metric: Δ_net = Δ_ambiguity - Δ_perturb (net ambiguity-specific effect).\n171\t      [Reviewer升级] 必须在 plan_002/003 full study 之前完成——\n172\t      如果 perturbation Δpp ≈ ambiguity Δpp，2,400 episodes 全部无效。\n173\t      低成本验证（30 pairs + 120 episodes API）优先于高成本投入。\n174\t      [判定标准 — 5 档]:\n175\t      PASS: Δ_perturb < 5pp (CI含0), ratio < 0.15 → C1 因果 claim 最强形式\n176\t      PASS+caveat: 5-10pp, ratio 0.15-0.30 → 报告 perturbation baseline, C1 写 net effect\n177\t      CONDITIONAL: 10-15pp, ratio 0.30-0.45 → 需 Δ_net > 20pp 且显著才可发表\n178\t      WARNING: 15-20pp, ratio 0.45-0.60 → C1 改为 \"additional violations beyond sensitivity\"\n179\t      FAIL: > 20pp, ratio > 0.60 → 无法声称 ambiguity-specific, 需根本重新设计\n180\t      [Power 注意]: N=120 对 10pp 差异 power ≈ 30%. 用 CI 宽度判定, 非 p-value.\n181\t      若 CI 过宽(>15pp width), 追加 60 episodes 压窄至 <10pp width.\n182\t      输出标准化 verdict 文件: perturbation_Δpp, ambiguity_Δpp, net_Δpp, CI, ratio, verdict.\n183\t    priority: P0\n184\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n185\t    deps: [plan_001]\n186\t    status: planned\n187\t\n188\t  # === P2: Nice to have ===\n189\t\n190\t  - id: plan_008\n191\t    name: classifier_poc\n192\t    claim: \"practical contribution\"\n193\t    description: >\n194\t      Binary ambiguity detector PoC: fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large on\n195\t      annotated clause pairs (ambiguous/unambiguous labels). Eval on\n196\t      held-out set. Demonstrates practical applicability of findings.\n197\t      Phase 3 from IDEA_BRIEF, scoped to PoC for EMNLP.\n198\t    priority: P2\n199\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n200\t    deps: [plan_001]\n201\t    status: planned\n202\t\n203\t# Resource summary:\n204\t# P0 GPU: 0h (plan_003 pivoted to API — no GPU needed)\n205\t# P1 GPU: 15h (plan_006 reliability local portion — can also go API)\n206\t# P2 GPU: 8h (plan_008 classifier fine-tuning)\n207\t# Total GPU: 8-23h (P2 only essential; P1 optional if API covers it)\n208\t# API cost: ~$450-700 (1,800 plan_002 + 1,200 plan_003 via OpenRouter + 720 reliability + 180 perturbation + judge cal)\n209\t# Models (all API via OpenRouter proxy at 47.94.22.126/v1):\n210\t#   gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1 (OpenAI, no prefix needed)\n211\t#   anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6 (Anthropic, prefix required)\n212\t#   qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b (Alibaba, open-source MoE, prefix required)\n213\t#   deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324 (DeepSeek, open-source, prefix required)\n214\t# [2026-05-20] Pivoted from local GPU to all-API: OpenRouter supports all 5 models\n215\t# [2026-05-20] Benchmark: τ²-bench (Barres et al. 2025, arXiv:2506.07982)\n216\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02e730a9-c151-4a4f-a6cc-efb839d223f7","uuid":"83734e75-5ba6-4c87-8fc1-cd552e643c95","timestamp":"2026-05-21T04:38:19.595Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/experiment_plan.yaml","content":"# Experiment Plan — policy_ambiguity_safety\n# Post-MVP, targeting EMNLP 2026 (ARR Aug cycle)\n# Claims reference paper_framing.md\n\nexperiments:\n  # === P0: Must-run for paper ===\n\n  - id: plan_001\n    name: full_study_clause_generation\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3\"\n    description: >\n      Generate remaining clauses for full study: coreferential (50 new),\n      authorization_scope (50 new), lexical (+20 to reach 50),\n      incompleteness (+20 to reach 50). Total 140 new clauses.\n      Validate all 300 clauses (50/type × 6 types) for completeness\n      and cross-type balance. Mix CP format per Reviewer suggestion\n      (labeled + unlabeled).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: []\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_001b\n    name: new_type_mini_pilot\n    claim: \"C1 (validation)\"\n    description: >\n      Mini-pilot for coreferential + authorization_scope (never tested):\n      5 clauses/type × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes.\n      Verify: (a) ambiguous triggers violations (b) unambiguous control < 15%.\n      If systematic issues found, fix clause design before full study.\n      API cost negligible (~$2). Per Reviewer warning on untested types.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_002\n    name: full_study_api\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4, C5\"\n    description: >\n      Run 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1,\n      claude-sonnet-4-6) = 1,800 episodes on τ²-bench. Cross-judge\n      evaluation. Output: episodes.jsonl + judgments.jsonl. No GPU needed.\n      Claude via OpenRouter proxy (base_url=http://47.94.22.126/v1).\n      [2026-05-20] Claude added per distill gap (4/8 papers use Claude baseline).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_001b, plan_010]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_003\n    name: full_study_opensource\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4, C5\"\n    description: >\n      Run 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models via OpenRouter API:\n      qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b (235B MoE, Alibaba) + deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324\n      (DeepSeek) = 1,200 episodes on τ²-bench. Cross-judge uses API models.\n      Can run in parallel with plan_002. No GPU needed.\n      [2026-05-20] Pivoted from local GPU → API: OpenRouter proxy confirmed\n      to support Qwen3 and DeepSeek models. Eliminates 48h GPU requirement.\n      Provider prefix required (e.g. qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b, not qwen3-235b-a22b).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_004\n    name: full_study_analysis\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4\"\n    description: >\n      Statistical analysis of full study data (3,000 episodes):\n      (a) Binary effect per type with bootstrap CI (C1)\n      (b) Omnibus χ² + pairwise across 6 types (C2)\n      (c) Visibility comparison: CP vs scopal rates (C3)\n      (d) Model × type interaction: 5×6 contingency + logistic regression (C4)\n      Report effect sizes + CI for all comparisons per Reviewer suggestion.\n      [Dream A3] Power analysis: report MDE for C2 (given N=250/type pooled)\n      and C3 (given N=250 per type). If V < 0.20 but MDE > observed V,\n      discuss underpowered possibility.\n      [Dream A4] TOST equivalence test with both ±15pp and ±10pp margins.\n      Justify margin choice explicitly.\n      [Dream A10] Report per-type information delta (token count difference\n      between ambiguous and unambiguous variants) as control variable.\n      [Dream B&K] Inter-model agreement on ambiguous clauses: do 5 models\n      adopt same or different interpretations? (supplementary analysis)\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_005\n    name: error_analysis\n    claim: \"C5\"\n    description: >\n      Qualitative analysis of agent traces from full study:\n      (a) Sample 50 violation traces per type (300 total)\n      (b) Classify failure modes (scope misapplication, conservative refusal,\n          assumption-based action, arbitrary rule selection, etc.)\n      (c) Cross-type failure mode distribution\n      (d) Visibility mechanism: compare CP traces (explicit conflict detection\n          behavior) vs scopal traces (surface scope adoption without awareness)\n      (e) Model-specific failure patterns (connect to C4)\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n    status: planned\n\n  # === P1: Important for robustness ===\n\n  - id: plan_006\n    name: reliability_test\n    claim: \"C1, C2\"\n    description: >\n      Test-retest reliability: select 30 representative clauses (5/type),\n      run 3 independent replicates × 2 conditions × 2 API models (gpt-5.4,\n      gpt-4.1) = 360 episodes. Local models added when plan_003 GPU available.\n      Compute ICC for per-clause violation rates. Addresses Reviewer warning\n      about ±8pp sampling noise (scopal 51.7% → 43.3% across MVP/diag).\n      Bootstrap CI width should be < 10pp for key comparisons.\n      [2026-05-20] API portion: 330/360 episodes complete (28/30 clauses),\n      judgments pending.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_007\n    name: realism_validation\n    claim: \"C1 (methodological)\"\n    description: >\n      Validate synthetic ambiguity injection realism:\n      (a) Linguistic property comparison with DRIP-R natural ambiguities\n          (sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR) + KS tests\n      (b) Optional: discriminator test if DRIP-R data accessible\n      Addresses RC4 (ecological validity).\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_009\n    name: judge_calibration\n    claim: \"C1 (methodological)\"\n    description: >\n      LLM-as-judge calibration per distilled research norm (5/8 papers):\n      (a) Sample 100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition\n      (b) Human expert labels (2 annotators, target κ ≥ 0.75)\n      (c) Compute judge precision/recall/F1 against human ground truth\n      (d) Per-severity-tier agreement rates\n      (e) Report in Method section as standard practice per AgentAuditor/DRIP-R\n      [Dream A7] Upgraded P1→P0: Dream best-tier reviewers identified this\n      as \"single most critical missing validation.\" Without it, entire\n      measurement chain from episode to violation label is unvalidated.\n      κ=0.91 measures LLM-LLM agreement, not accuracy.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_010\n    name: perturbation_control\n    claim: \"C1 (causal validity)\"\n    description: >\n      [Dream A9] Non-ambiguity perturbation control arm to distinguish\n      ambiguity-specific harm from general prompt brittleness.\n      Generate 30 clause pairs with non-ambiguity perturbations:\n      (a) 15 synonym substitution pairs (replace key terms with synonyms)\n      (b) 15 clause reordering pairs (reorder conditions without changing meaning)\n      Run 30 × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6) = 180 episodes.\n      Key metric: Δ_net = Δ_ambiguity - Δ_perturb (net ambiguity-specific effect).\n      [Reviewer升级] 必须在 plan_002/003 full study 之前完成——\n      如果 perturbation Δpp ≈ ambiguity Δpp，2,400 episodes 全部无效。\n      低成本验证（30 pairs + 120 episodes API）优先于高成本投入。\n      [判定标准 — 5 档]:\n      PASS: Δ_perturb < 5pp (CI含0), ratio < 0.15 → C1 因果 claim 最强形式\n      PASS+caveat: 5-10pp, ratio 0.15-0.30 → 报告 perturbation baseline, C1 写 net effect\n      CONDITIONAL: 10-15pp, ratio 0.30-0.45 → 需 Δ_net > 20pp 且显著才可发表\n      WARNING: 15-20pp, ratio 0.45-0.60 → C1 改为 \"additional violations beyond sensitivity\"\n      FAIL: > 20pp, ratio > 0.60 → 无法声称 ambiguity-specific, 需根本重新设计\n      [Power 注意]: N=120 对 10pp 差异 power ≈ 30%. 用 CI 宽度判定, 非 p-value.\n      若 CI 过宽(>15pp width), 追加 60 episodes 压窄至 <10pp width.\n      输出标准化 verdict 文件: perturbation_Δpp, ambiguity_Δpp, net_Δpp, CI, ratio, verdict.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  # === P2: Nice to have ===\n\n  - id: plan_008\n    name: classifier_poc\n    claim: \"practical contribution\"\n    description: >\n      Binary ambiguity detector PoC: fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large on\n      annotated clause pairs (ambiguous/unambiguous labels). Eval on\n      held-out set. Demonstrates practical applicability of findings.\n      Phase 3 from IDEA_BRIEF, scoped to PoC for EMNLP.\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n# Resource summary:\n# P0 GPU: 0h (plan_003 pivoted to API — no GPU needed)\n# P1 GPU: 15h (plan_006 reliability local portion — can also go API)\n# P2 GPU: 8h (plan_008 classifier fine-tuning)\n# Total GPU: 8-23h (P2 only essential; P1 optional if API covers it)\n# API cost: ~$450-700 (1,800 plan_002 + 1,200 plan_003 via OpenRouter + 720 reliability + 180 perturbation + judge cal)\n# Models (all API via OpenRouter proxy at 47.94.22.126/v1):\n#   gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1 (OpenAI, no prefix needed)\n#   anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6 (Anthropic, prefix required)\n#   qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b (Alibaba, open-source MoE, prefix required)\n#   deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324 (DeepSeek, open-source, prefix required)\n# [2026-05-20] Pivoted from local GPU to all-API: OpenRouter supports all 5 models\n# [2026-05-20] Benchmark: τ²-bench (Barres et al. 2025, arXiv:2506.07982)\n","numLines":216,"startLine":1,"totalLines":216}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018BGviF2griaJcrgmfFk1t8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\ttier: worst\n2\tnarrative_guidance: 'Layer hierarchy 无法作为 headline claim。5-model pooled layer gap\n3\t  仅 ~4pp (p=0.14, n.s.)， 被 model×type interaction (p=0.008) 瓦解——type ranking 因模型架构而异\n4\t  (GPT 系 spec>ling, Qwen3-8B 反转, Claude 混合)。Judge calibration 暴露 coreferential (F1=0.61)\n5\t  和 auth_scope (F1=0.68) 的 type-specific measurement bias， 进一步削弱 type-level claims。Error\n6\t  analysis failure mode 跨层重叠 42%，无 clean mechanism 区分。 首选 reframe: (C) \"The Massive\n7\t  Binary Effect\" 为 primary——+30pp 仍是文献最大因果效应 + perturbation control PASS (Δ=4.2pp,\n8\t  ratio=0.13)；(B) \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 为 §6 核心—— 92% traces 中 agent 未识别歧义存在，universal\n9\t  across types and models。 C2 降级为 \"Model-Dependent Vulnerability Profiles\" (model×type\n10\t  interaction 从 nuisance 升级为 finding)； C3 layer claim 放弃。备选标题: \"Policy Ambiguity Causes\n11\t  Catastrophic Safety Violations in LLM Agents: A Causal Study\"。仍投 EMNLP——C1 (causal\n12\t  binary effect) + perturbation control + ambiguity blindness analysis = solid 3-contribution\n13\t  paper。\n14\t\n15\t  '\n16\timagined_experiments:\n17\t- name: full_study_clause_generation\n18\t  plan_id: plan_001\n19\t  description: '生成 140 新 clause pairs (coreferential 50, auth_scope 50, lexical +20,\n20\t    incompleteness +20)， 补全 6 types × 50 pairs = 300 对。混合 CP 格式 (labeled + unlabeled)。Chantree-style\n21\t    质量验证。\n22\t\n23\t    '\n24\t  expected_results:\n25\t    total_pairs: 300\n26\t    pairs_per_type: 50\n27\t    cp_labeled_ratio: 0.5\n28\t    quality_pass_rate: 0.92\n29\t    avg_token_delta_amb_vs_unamb: 3.8\n30\t    coreferential_revision_rounds: 3\n31\t    auth_scope_revision_rounds: 2\n32\t  result_rationale: 'Clause 生成本身不受 worst tier 影响——数据准备阶段。但 quality_pass_rate 92% 而非\n33\t    >95% 因为 coreferential 的 RC attachment 与 scopal 存在边界重叠 (RC8 预示的问题)， 以及 auth_scope\n34\t    与 incompleteness 的 distinction 需要精细控制 (RC9)。 Coreferential 需要 3 轮修订 (vs 常规 1-2\n35\t    轮)：mini-pilot 会暴露 2/5 clauses 触发 conservative refusal 而非 violation，需重写。这些 clause\n36\t    层面的质量差异 会在后续实验中放大为 type-specific measurement noise。\n37\t\n38\t    '\n39\t  tables:\n40\t  - name: Clause Pair Statistics by Type\n41\t    columns:\n42\t    - type\n43\t    - n_pairs\n44\t    - avg_amb_tokens\n45\t    - avg_unamb_tokens\n46\t    - token_delta\n47\t    - quality_pass_rate\n48\t    rows:\n49\t    - - auth_scope\n50\t      - 50\n51\t      - 28.3\n52\t      - 32.1\n53\t      - 3.8\n54\t      - 0.9\n55\t    - - incompleteness\n56\t      - 50\n57\t      - 26.7\n58\t      - 30.5\n59\t      - 3.8\n60\t      - 0.94\n61\t    - - conditional_polysemy\n62\t      - 50\n63\t      - 24.2\n64\t      - 25.8\n65\t      - 1.6\n66\t      - 0.96\n67\t    - - scopal\n68\t      - 50\n69\t      - 22.5\n70\t      - 23.9\n71\t      - 1.4\n72\t      - 0.96\n73\t    - - lexical\n74\t      - 50\n75\t      - 21.8\n76\t      - 23.1\n77\t      - 1.3\n78\t      - 0.94\n79\t    - - coreferential\n80\t      - 50\n81\t      - 25.1\n82\t      - 27.4\n83\t      - 2.3\n84\t      - 0.88\n85\t  figures_description:\n86\t  - 'Token length distribution per type (box plot): spec-layer types 系统性更长，unambiguous\n87\t    版本需更多 explicit information'\n88\t  analysis: 'Coreferential quality_pass_rate 最低 (0.88)，auth_scope 0.90——这两个新 type\n89\t    的 clause 质量问题会在 plan_009 judge calibration 中以 type-specific F1 下降的形式体现。 Token\n90\t    delta spec-layer (3.8) > ling-layer (1.7) 是 potential confound， plan_004 需 report\n91\t    并控制。\n92\t\n93\t    '\n94\t- name: new_type_mini_pilot\n95\t  plan_id: plan_001b\n96\t  description: 'Coreferential + auth_scope 各 5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4)\n97\t    = 20 episodes。 验证新类型基本可行性。\n98\t\n99\t    '\n100\t  expected_results:\n101\t    coreferential_amb_violation_rate: 0.4\n102\t    coreferential_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n103\t    auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.6\n104\t    auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n105\t    coreferential_binary_effect_pp: 40\n106\t    auth_scope_binary_effect_pp: 60\n107\t    systematic_issues_found: true\n108\t    issues_detail: 2/5 coreferential clauses 触发 conservative refusal 而非 violation;\n109\t      1/5 auth_scope unambiguous 版本仍残余歧义\n110\t  result_rationale: 'Mini-pilot 在 gpt-5.4 上给出 \"go\" 信号——两个新 type 均触发 violations，control\n111\t    < 15%。 但这是 worst tier 的隐患起点: gpt-5.4 的 auth_scope 60% / coreferential 40% pattern\n112\t    看似 confirm spec > ling hierarchy，但 N=5 的 CI 极宽 (±30pp)。 关键: 相同 clauses 在 Qwen3-8B\n113\t    上 profile 会反转 (coreferential ~45%, auth_scope ~28%)—— mini-pilot 仅测 1 model 无法预见跨模型\n114\t    interaction。 gpt-5.4 上 coreferential 2/5 conservative refusal 预示该 type 行为异质性高，\n115\t    但在 mini-pilot 被归为 \"fixable clause quality issue\" 而非 structural warning。\n116\t\n117\t    '\n118\t  tables:\n119\t  - name: Mini-Pilot Results\n120\t    columns:\n121\t    - type\n122\t    - condition\n123\t    - n\n124\t    - violations\n125\t    - rate\n126\t    rows:\n127\t    - - coreferential\n128\t      - ambiguous\n129\t      - 5\n130\t      - 2\n131\t      - 40%\n132\t    - - coreferential\n133\t      - unambiguous\n134\t      - 5\n135\t      - 0\n136\t      - 0%\n137\t    - - auth_scope\n138\t      - ambiguous\n139\t      - 5\n140\t      - 3\n141\t      - 60%\n142\t    - - auth_scope\n143\t      - unambiguous\n144\t      - 5\n145\t      - 0\n146\t      - 0%\n147\t  figures_description: []\n148\t  analysis: 'Mini-pilot 的 \"go\" 信号在 worst tier 下是 misleading confidence: gpt-5.4 single-model\n149\t    validation 无法检测 model-dependent vulnerability profiles。 实际需要 ≥2 model families\n150\t    的 mini-pilot 才能预见 plan_003 的 interaction 问题。\n151\t\n152\t    '\n153\t- name: perturbation_control\n154\t  plan_id: plan_010\n155\t  description: '30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs (15 synonym substitution + 15\n156\t    clause reordering) × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 180 episodes。验证 ambiguity-specific\n157\t    因果性。\n158\t\n159\t    '\n160\t  expected_results:\n161\t    total_episodes: 180\n162\t    perturbation_delta_pp: 4.2\n163\t    perturbation_ci: '[-1.8, 10.2]'\n164\t    ambiguity_delta_pp: 31.5\n165\t    ambiguity_ci: '[26.8, 36.2]'\n166\t    net_delta_pp: 27.3\n167\t    ratio: 0.13\n168\t    verdict: PASS\n169\t    synonym_substitution_delta_pp: 3.1\n170\t    synonym_ci: '[-3.2, 9.4]'\n171\t    clause_reordering_delta_pp: 5.3\n172\t    clause_reordering_ci: '[-0.8, 11.4]'\n173\t    ci_width_perturbation: 12.0\n174\t  result_rationale: 'Perturbation control 在 worst tier 下仍 PASS——binary effect 的因果性不受\n175\t    layer hierarchy 问题影响。 Δ_perturb=4.2pp (CI 含 0): synonym substitution (3.1pp) 和\n176\t    clause reordering (5.3pp) 均不引起 meaningful violation rate 变化。Ratio=0.13 < 0.15\n177\t    → PASS 最强形式。 Clause reordering 略高 (5.3pp) 源于轻微 primacy/recency effect，但远小于 ambiguity\n178\t    effect。 CI width 12.0pp 接近但未超过 15pp 追加阈值——worst tier 下这是 marginal 风险， 但当前数据足够。这个\n179\t    PASS 是 worst tier 的最大 silver lining: 即使 type hierarchy 崩溃，binary ambiguity effect\n180\t    仍有最强因果证据支撑， 使 reframe (C) \"Massive Binary Effect\" 有坚实因果基础。\n181\t\n182\t    '\n183\t  tables:\n184\t  - name: Perturbation Control Results\n185\t    columns:\n186\t    - condition\n187\t    - violation_rate\n188\t    - Δpp_vs_baseline\n189\t    - 95% CI\n190\t    rows:\n191\t    - - unambiguous_baseline\n192\t      - 5.5%\n193\t      - —\n194\t      - —\n195\t    - - synonym_substitution\n196\t      - 8.6%\n197\t      - +3.1pp\n198\t      - '[-3.2, 9.4]'\n199\t    - - clause_reordering\n200\t      - 10.8%\n201\t      - +5.3pp\n202\t      - '[-0.8, 11.4]'\n203\t    - - perturbation_pooled\n204\t      - 9.7%\n205\t      - +4.2pp\n206\t      - '[-1.8, 10.2]'\n207\t    - - ambiguous\n208\t      - 37.0%\n209\t      - +31.5pp\n210\t      - '[26.8, 36.2]'\n211\t  - name: Perturbation Verdict Summary\n212\t    columns:\n213\t    - metric\n214\t    - value\n215\t    - threshold\n216\t    - verdict\n217\t    rows:\n218\t    - - Δ_perturb\n219\t      - 4.2pp\n220\t      - < 5pp\n221\t      - ✓ PASS\n222\t    - - ratio\n223\t      - '0.13'\n224\t      - < 0.15\n225\t      - ✓ PASS\n226\t    - - CI_contains_0\n227\t      - 'yes'\n228\t      - required\n229\t      - ✓\n230\t    - - CI_width\n231\t      - 12.0pp\n232\t      - < 15pp\n233\t      - ✓ (marginal)\n234\t  figures_description:\n235\t  - 'Bar chart: baseline / perturbation / ambiguity 三条件 violation rate + CI — ambiguity\n236\t    远超其余两条件'\n237\t  analysis: 'PASS verdict 确保 C1 因果 claim 在任何 tier 下成立。 这是 paper 的 methodological backbone——区别于所有\n238\t    prior work (DRIP-R, PhantomPolicy 均无此控制)。\n239\t\n240\t    '\n241\t- name: full_study_api\n242\t  plan_id: plan_002\n243\t  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6)\n244\t    = 1,800 episodes。 在原 2-model 基础上新增 Claude。Cross-judge evaluation。\n245\t\n246\t    '\n247\t  expected_results:\n248\t    total_episodes: 1800\n249\t    gpt54_rates:\n250\t      auth_scope: 0.55\n251\t      incompleteness: 0.52\n252\t      cp: 0.35\n253\t      scopal: 0.4\n254\t      lexical: 0.38\n255\t      coreferential: 0.25\n256\t    gpt41_rates:\n257\t      auth_scope: 0.53\n258\t      incompleteness: 0.5\n259\t      cp: 0.34\n260\t      scopal: 0.39\n261\t      lexical: 0.36\n262\t      coreferential: 0.24\n263\t    claude_rates:\n264\t      auth_scope: 0.38\n265\t      incompleteness: 0.36\n266\t      cp: 0.28\n267\t      scopal: 0.33\n268\t      lexical: 0.3\n269\t      coreferential: 0.42\n270\t    gpt54_binary_effect_pp: 36.2\n271\t    gpt41_binary_effect_pp: 34.0\n272\t    claude_binary_effect_pp: 26.5\n273\t    gpt54_layer_gap_pp: 13.0\n274\t    gpt41_layer_gap_pp: 12.7\n275\t    claude_layer_gap_pp: -1.0\n276\t    binary_effect_3api_pp: 32.7\n277\t    layer_gap_3api_pp: 8.2\n278\t    cramers_v_3api: 0.15\n279\t    model_main_effect_p_3api: 0.004\n280\t    model_type_interaction_p_3api: 0.018\n281\t    avg_unamb_rate_3api: 0.055\n282\t    claude_unamb_rate: 0.08\n283\t    claude_amb_avg: 0.345\n284\t  result_rationale: 'GPT 系 (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) 复现 plan_002 原始 pattern: spec >> ling，两模型高度一致\n285\t    (rank ρ=0.94)。GPT 对 authorization boundary 和 incompleteness 的 pragmatic underspecification\n286\t    高度敏感——缺乏 explicit permission 时倾向 assume-and-act。\n287\t\n288\t    Claude 展现截然不同的 vulnerability profile——worst tier 的第一个转折点: (a) auth_scope/incompleteness\n289\t    显著低 (38%/36% vs GPT 55%/52%): Claude RLHF 训练 强化了 \"不确定时 refuse\" 的行为，specification-layer\n290\t    ambiguity 更多触发 refusal 而非 violation。 (b) coreferential 显著高 (42% vs GPT 25%): Claude\n291\t    在 RC attachment 歧义上 系统性选择 wider-scope interpretation (执行而非收窄)。RC attachment 不触发\n292\t    Claude 的 safety refusal mechanism (与 auth boundary 不同)，因此 Claude 在此 \"放松警惕\"。 (c)\n293\t    结果: Claude layer gap 反转 (ling 35.0% > spec 34.0%)。 3-API pooled layer gap 从 2-model\n294\t    的 19pp 压缩至 8.2pp。\n295\t\n296\t    Model×type interaction 已在 3 API 模型中显著 (p=0.018)—— 尚未加入 Qwen 就已可见 type ranking\n297\t    非 universal。 Claude binary effect 仅 +26.5pp: 整体更保守 (unamb baseline 8% vs GPT ~4.5%),\n298\t    ambiguous 条件下更多 refuse/ask 而非 violate。\n299\t\n300\t    '\n301\t  tables:\n302\t  - name: Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Ambiguous Condition)\n303\t    columns:\n304\t    - type\n305\t    - layer\n306\t    - gpt-5.4\n307\t    - gpt-4.1\n308\t    - claude-sonnet-4-6\n309\t    - 3-API_pooled\n310\t    rows:\n311\t    - - auth_scope\n312\t      - spec\n313\t      - 55%\n314\t      - 53%\n315\t      - 38%\n316\t      - 48.7%\n317\t    - - incompleteness\n318\t      - spec\n319\t      - 52%\n320\t      - 50%\n321\t      - 36%\n322\t      - 46.0%\n323\t    - - cond_polysemy\n324\t      - spec\n325\t      - 35%\n326\t      - 34%\n327\t      - 28%\n328\t      - 32.3%\n329\t    - - scopal\n330\t      - ling\n331\t      - 40%\n332\t      - 39%\n333\t      - 33%\n334\t      - 37.3%\n335\t    - - lexical\n336\t      - ling\n337\t      - 38%\n338\t      - 36%\n339\t      - 30%\n340\t      - 34.7%\n341\t    - - coreferential\n342\t      - ling\n343\t      - 25%\n344\t      - 24%\n345\t      - 42%\n346\t      - 30.3%\n347\t    - - spec_avg\n348\t      - —\n349\t      - 47.3%\n350\t      - 45.7%\n351\t      - 34.0%\n352\t      - 42.3%\n353\t    - - ling_avg\n354\t      - —\n355\t      - 34.3%\n356\t      - 33.0%\n357\t      - 35.0%\n358\t      - 34.1%\n359\t    - - layer_gap\n360\t      - —\n361\t      - +13.0pp\n362\t      - +12.7pp\n363\t      - -1.0pp\n364\t      - +8.2pp\n365\t  - name: Binary Effect by API Model\n366\t    columns:\n367\t    - model\n368\t    - amb_rate\n369\t    - unamb_rate\n370\t    - Δpp\n371\t    - McNemar_OR\n372\t    - p\n373\t    rows:\n374\t    - - gpt-5.4\n375\t      - 40.8%\n376\t      - 4.6%\n377\t      - +36.2pp\n378\t      - 38.5\n379\t      - <0.0001\n380\t    - - gpt-4.1\n381\t      - 39.3%\n382\t      - 5.3%\n383\t      - +34.0pp\n384\t      - 31.2\n385\t      - <0.0001\n386\t    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n387\t      - 34.5%\n388\t      - 8.0%\n389\t      - +26.5pp\n390\t      - 16.8\n391\t      - <0.0001\n392\t    - - 3-API_pooled\n393\t      - 38.2%\n394\t      - 5.5%\n395\t      - +32.7pp\n396\t      - 28.4\n397\t      - <0.0001\n398\t  figures_description:\n399\t  - 'Heatmap 3×6: 清晰显示 Claude coreferential 异常高 (42%) 与 auth_scope 异常低 (38%)——与 GPT\n400\t    系对角相反'\n401\t  - 'Forest plot: per-type binary effect by model with 95% CI — Claude CI 与 GPT 不重叠\n402\t    (auth_scope, coreferential)'\n403\t  analysis: 'Claude 的加入将 3-API layer gap 压缩至 8.2pp (从 2-model 19pp)。 model×type interaction\n404\t    已显著 (p=0.018)——plan_003 加入 Qwen 后会进一步恶化。 Claude 的 coreferential 高 rate 机制: RLHF\n405\t    的 safety training 覆盖了 authorization-class violations 但不覆盖 referential-class misinterpretation，导致\n406\t    asymmetric vulnerability。 C3 (universal layer hierarchy) 在此阶段已不可维持。\n407\t\n408\t    '\n409\t- name: full_study_local\n410\t  plan_id: plan_003\n411\t  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n412\t    via vLLM) = 1,200 episodes。 48 GPU-hours on RTX PRO 6000。\n413\t\n414\t    '\n415\t  expected_results:\n416\t    total_episodes: 1200\n417\t    qwen8b_rates:\n418\t      auth_scope: 0.28\n419\t      incompleteness: 0.3\n420\t      cp: 0.25\n421\t      scopal: 0.32\n422\t      lexical: 0.3\n423\t      coreferential: 0.45\n424\t    qwen8b_binary_effect_pp: 23.7\n425\t    qwen8b_unamb_rate: 0.08\n426\t    qwen8b_amb_avg: 0.317\n427\t    qwen8b_layer_gap_pp: -8.0\n428\t    qwen8b_spec_avg: 0.277\n429\t    qwen8b_ling_avg: 0.357\n430\t    qwen32b_rates:\n431\t      auth_scope: 0.4\n432\t      incompleteness: 0.42\n433\t      cp: 0.3\n434\t      scopal: 0.35\n435\t      lexical: 0.33\n436\t      coreferential: 0.38\n437\t    qwen32b_binary_effect_pp: 30.3\n438\t    qwen32b_unamb_rate: 0.06\n439\t    qwen32b_amb_avg: 0.363\n440\t    qwen32b_layer_gap_pp: 2.0\n441\t    qwen32b_spec_avg: 0.373\n442\t    qwen32b_ling_avg: 0.353\n443\t    binary_effect_2local_pp: 27.0\n444\t    layer_gap_2local_pp: -3.0\n445\t    model_type_interaction_2local_p: 0.041\n446\t  result_rationale: 'Qwen3-8B 是 worst tier 的关键变量——vulnerability profile 质变:\n447\t\n448\t    (a) Auth_scope 仅 28% (GPT-5.4 的一半): 8B 参数模型缺乏 pragmatic reasoning 能力， 无法 \"推断\"\n449\t    implicit permission boundary 并据此行动——不是因为保守 refuse (像 Claude)， 而是因为根本不理解 authorization\n450\t    的 pragmatic implication，倾向 ignore 或 default 行为。 低 auth_scope violation ≠ 安全，只是不同的\n451\t    failure mode (inaction vs wrong action)。\n452\t\n453\t    (b) Coreferential 高达 45% (GPT-5.4 的 1.8 倍): 小模型更依赖 surface syntactic heuristics\n454\t    (如 left-attachment bias for RC)。GPT-5.4 能利用 tool response 做部分 disambiguation (Berry\n455\t    & Kamsties 的 \"disambiguation channel\")，Qwen3-8B 不具备此能力—— 对 linguistic-layer 反而更脆弱。\n456\t\n457\t    (c) Layer gap 反转至 -8pp (ling 35.7% > spec 27.7%): 完全颠覆 GPT 的 spec > ling pattern。\n458\t    机制: 小模型的 pragmatic processing 不足使 spec-layer 失去 \"特别危险\" 的地位， 而 syntactic processing\n459\t    的 surface heuristic 依赖使 ling-layer 变得更危险。\n460\t\n461\t    Qwen3-32B-AWQ 居中 (gap +2pp, nearly flat): scale 部分恢复了 spec-layer sensitivity，\n462\t    但未达 GPT 水平。AWQ 4-bit 量化可能引入额外 noise 但不改变 qualitative pattern。 这支持 \"layer gap 是\n463\t    emergent capability\"——需要足够的 pragmatic reasoning 能力 才能 \"解锁\" specification-layer\n464\t    的特殊危险性。\n465\t\n466\t    '\n467\t  tables:\n468\t  - name: Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Local Models, Ambiguous)\n469\t    columns:\n470\t    - type\n471\t    - layer\n472\t    - Qwen3-8B\n473\t    - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n474\t    - 2-local_pooled\n475\t    rows:\n476\t    - - auth_scope\n477\t      - spec\n478\t      - 28%\n479\t      - 40%\n480\t      - 34.0%\n481\t    - - incompleteness\n482\t      - spec\n483\t      - 30%\n484\t      - 42%\n485\t      - 36.0%\n486\t    - - cond_polysemy\n487\t      - spec\n488\t      - 25%\n489\t      - 30%\n490\t      - 27.5%\n491\t    - - scopal\n492\t      - ling\n493\t      - 32%\n494\t      - 35%\n495\t      - 33.5%\n496\t    - - lexical\n497\t      - ling\n498\t      - 30%\n499\t      - 33%\n500\t      - 31.5%\n501\t    - - coreferential\n502\t      - ling\n503\t      - 45%\n504\t      - 38%\n505\t      - 41.5%\n506\t    - - spec_avg\n507\t      - —\n508\t      - 27.7%\n509\t      - 37.3%\n510\t      - 32.5%\n511\t    - - ling_avg\n512\t      - —\n513\t      - 35.7%\n514\t      - 35.3%\n515\t      - 35.5%\n516\t    - - layer_gap\n517\t      - —\n518\t      - -8.0pp\n519\t      - +2.0pp\n520\t      - -3.0pp\n521\t  - name: Binary Effect by Local Model\n522\t    columns:\n523\t    - model\n524\t    - amb_rate\n525\t    - unamb_rate\n526\t    - Δpp\n527\t    - McNemar_OR\n528\t    - p\n529\t    rows:\n530\t    - - Qwen3-8B\n531\t      - 31.7%\n532\t      - 8.0%\n533\t      - +23.7pp\n534\t      - 9.4\n535\t      - <0.0001\n536\t    - - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n537\t      - 36.3%\n538\t      - 6.0%\n539\t      - +30.3pp\n540\t      - 21.7\n541\t      - <0.0001\n542\t  figures_description:\n543\t  - 'Radar chart 5 models × 6 types: Qwen3-8B profile 与 GPT 系近似镜像——coreferential 峰值、auth_scope\n544\t    谷底'\n545\t  - 'Layer gap by model bar chart: GPT 正、Claude/Qwen3-32B 近零、Qwen3-8B 负——gradient\n546\t    随 model capability'\n547\t  analysis: 'Qwen3-8B 的 reversed layer profile 是 worst tier 的 smoking gun。 与 GPT-5.4\n548\t    的 type rank Spearman ρ=0.37 (weak)——两个模型本质上有不同的 vulnerability landscape。 Qwen3-32B\n549\t    的 ρ=0.77 (moderate) 说明 scale 恢复了部分 alignment，但未完全收敛。 Binary effect 仍显著 (Qwen3-8B\n550\t    +23.7pp, p<0.0001)——ambiguity 对所有模型都有害， 但 \"哪种 ambiguity 更有害\" 取决于模型能力。\n551\t\n552\t    '\n553\t- name: full_study_analysis\n554\t  plan_id: plan_004\n555\t  description: '3,000 episodes 统计分析: C1 binary effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer\n556\t    effect, C4 model×type interaction, power analysis, TOST, inter-model agreement,\n557\t    information delta control。\n558\t\n559\t    '\n560\t  expected_results:\n561\t    binary_effect_5model_pp: 30.2\n562\t    binary_effect_5model_ci: '[27.5, 32.9]'\n563\t    mcnemar_or_5model: 24.1\n564\t    mcnemar_or_ci: '[16.3, 35.6]'\n565\t    mcnemar_p: <0.0001\n566\t    per_type_all_significant: true\n567\t    weakest_type_effect: coreferential +22.8pp (Qwen3-8B drags avg down from +16pp\n568\t      to... wait, UP — Qwen3-8B has high coreferential)\n569\t    omnibus_chi2_5model: 18.7\n570\t    omnibus_p_5model: 0.002\n571\t    cramers_v_5model: 0.11\n572\t    pooled_rates:\n573\t      auth_scope: 42.8%\n574\t      incompleteness: 42.0%\n575\t      cp: 30.4%\n576\t      scopal: 35.8%\n577\t      lexical: 33.4%\n578\t      coreferential: 34.8%\n579\t    spec_avg_5model: 38.4%\n580\t    ling_avg_5model: 34.7%\n581\t    layer_gap_5model_pp: 3.7\n582\t    layer_gap_ci: '[-1.2, 8.6]'\n583\t    layer_gap_p: 0.14\n584\t    model_type_interaction_chi2: 52.3\n585\t    model_type_interaction_p: 0.008\n586\t    model_type_interaction_v: 0.089\n587\t    model_main_effect_p: 0.001\n588\t    model_main_effect_v: 0.072\n589\t    interaction_lrt_chi2: 38.6\n590\t    interaction_lrt_p: 0.003\n591\t    interaction_lrt_df: 20\n592\t    rank_rho_gpt41: 0.94\n593\t    rank_rho_claude: 0.54\n594\t    rank_rho_qwen32b: 0.77\n595\t    rank_rho_qwen8b: 0.37\n596\t    tost_15pp_equivalent_pairs: 6/15\n597\t    tost_10pp_equivalent_pairs: 2/15\n598\t    mde_c2_v: 0.18\n599\t    mde_c3_pp: 9.5\n600\t    observed_c2_v: 0.11\n601\t    observed_c3_gap: 3.7\n602\t    fleiss_kappa_ambiguous: 0.62\n603\t    fleiss_kappa_unambiguous: 0.85\n604\t    same_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.58\n605\t    different_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.42\n606\t    avg_token_delta_spec: 3.4\n607\t    avg_token_delta_ling: 1.7\n608\t    token_delta_violation_corr: 0.31\n609\t    token_delta_partial_r_after_type: 0.14\n610\t  result_rationale: 'C1 (+30.2pp, CI [27.5, 32.9]): 从 plan_002 的 +36.5pp 下降 6pp。 原因:\n611\t    Qwen3-8B 的弱 binary effect (+23.7pp) 和 Claude 的 (+26.5pp) 拉低 pooled 值。 但 CI 远离零，OR=24.1\n612\t    仍 massive——文献中最大的 ambiguity → safety 因果效应。 Per-type 均显著 (最弱: CP +25.6pp)——\"所有\n613\t    ambiguity 都 nocuous\" 成立。\n614\t\n615\t    C2 (V=0.11, p=0.002): omnibus χ² 显著说明 types 不完全等价， 但 V=0.11 (weak) 远低于 plan_002\n616\t    2-model 的 V=0.207。 原因: open-source 模型的 reversed/flat profile 平均化了 type 间差异。 具体看:\n617\t    auth_scope/incompleteness 仍最高 (~43%)，但 coreferential 从 25% 跳至 34.8% (Claude 42%\n618\t    + Qwen3-8B 45% 拉高)，压缩了原本的 range。 TOST: ±15pp 有 6/15 pairs equivalent (原 3/15)——更多\n619\t    type pairs 在统计上不可区分。\n620\t\n621\t    C3 (gap 3.7pp, p=0.14, n.s.): layer gap 不显著。CI [-1.2, 8.6] 包含 0。 GPT 的 positive\n622\t    gap (~13pp) 被 Claude (-1pp) + Qwen3-8B (-8pp) 抵消。 MDE=9.5pp: 即使有 power，跨模型方向不一致使\n623\t    pooled estimate 本身无 interpretive value。 Layer hierarchy 从 \"finding\" 变为 \"GPT-family\n624\t    tendency\"。\n625\t\n626\t    C4 (interaction p=0.008): worst tier 最 informative finding。 5×6 contingency table\n627\t    中 model×type interaction 高度显著——type ranking 是 model-dependent。 Three distinct\n628\t    vulnerability profiles: - GPT family: spec-sensitive (auth_scope/incompleteness\n629\t    peak) - Claude: coreferential-sensitive (RLHF safety coverage gap) - Qwen3-8B:\n630\t    ling-sensitive (surface heuristic dependence) Spearman ρ gradient: GPT intra-family\n631\t    0.94 > Qwen3-32B 0.77 > Claude 0.54 > Qwen3-8B 0.37\n632\t\n633\t    Inter-model Fleiss κ=0.62 (ambiguous) vs 0.85 (unambiguous): 分歧主要在 ambiguous clauses——ambiguity\n634\t    暴露了 model-specific interpretation strategies。 58% same interpretation → 不是 true\n635\t    nocuity (divergent readings) 而是 systematic bias (models differ in fallback strategies\n636\t    when they can''t resolve ambiguity)。 Berry & Kamsties 框架下: 这是 \"systematic nocuity\"\n637\t    (所有模型都错但错法不同) 而非 \"divergent nocuity\" (不同解读)。\n638\t\n639\t    Token delta: spec-layer 3.4 vs ling-layer 1.7 tokens，与 violation rate 弱相关 (r=0.31)。\n640\t    但 partial correlation after controlling for type = 0.14 (n.s.)—— token delta 不是\n641\t    independent confound，与 type 共线。需 disclose 但不构成 fatal threat。\n642\t\n643\t    '\n644\t  tables:\n645\t  - name: 5-Model Pooled Per-Type Results\n646\t    columns:\n647\t    - type\n648\t    - layer\n649\t    - amb_rate\n650\t    - unamb_rate\n651\t    - Δpp\n652\t    - 95% CI\n653\t    - per-type McNemar p\n654\t    rows:\n655\t    - - auth_scope\n656\t      - spec\n657\t      - 42.8%\n658\t      - 5.8%\n659\t      - +37.0pp\n660\t      - '[31.2, 42.8]'\n661\t      - <0.0001\n662\t    - - incompleteness\n663\t      - spec\n664\t      - 42.0%\n665\t      - 5.4%\n666\t      - +36.6pp\n667\t      - '[30.8, 42.4]'\n668\t      - <0.0001\n669\t    - - cond_polysemy\n670\t      - spec\n671\t      - 30.4%\n672\t      - 4.8%\n673\t      - +25.6pp\n674\t      - '[20.1, 31.1]'\n675\t      - <0.0001\n676\t    - - scopal\n677\t      - ling\n678\t      - 35.8%\n679\t      - 5.6%\n680\t      - +30.2pp\n681\t      - '[24.5, 35.9]'\n682\t      - <0.0001\n683\t    - - lexical\n684\t      - ling\n685\t      - 33.4%\n686\t      - 5.2%\n687\t      - +28.2pp\n688\t      - '[22.6, 33.8]'\n689\t      - <0.0001\n690\t    - - coreferential\n691\t      - ling\n692\t      - 34.8%\n693\t      - 6.0%\n694\t      - +28.8pp\n695\t      - '[23.1, 34.5]'\n696\t      - <0.0001\n697\t  - name: Layer Effect by Model\n698\t    columns:\n699\t    - model\n700\t    - spec_avg\n701\t    - ling_avg\n702\t    - layer_gap_pp\n703\t    - direction\n704\t    rows:\n705\t    - - gpt-5.4\n706\t      - 47.3%\n707\t      - 34.3%\n708\t      - +13.0pp\n709\t      - spec > ling\n710\t    - - gpt-4.1\n711\t      - 45.7%\n712\t      - 33.0%\n713\t      - +12.7pp\n714\t      - spec > ling\n715\t    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n716\t      - 34.0%\n717\t      - 35.0%\n718\t      - -1.0pp\n719\t      - ≈ flat (reversed)\n720\t    - - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n721\t      - 37.3%\n722\t      - 35.3%\n723\t      - +2.0pp\n724\t      - ≈ flat\n725\t    - - Qwen3-8B\n726\t      - 27.7%\n727\t      - 35.7%\n728\t      - -8.0pp\n729\t      - ling > spec (reversed)\n730\t    - - 5-model_pooled\n731\t      - 38.4%\n732\t      - 34.7%\n733\t      - +3.7pp\n734\t      - n.s. (p=0.14)\n735\t  - name: 'Model × Type Interaction: Type Rank by Model (ambiguous violation rate)'\n736\t    columns:\n737\t    - rank\n738\t    - gpt-5.4\n739\t    - gpt-4.1\n740\t    - claude\n741\t    - Qwen3-32B\n742\t    - Qwen3-8B\n743\t    rows:\n744\t    - - 1 (highest)\n745\t      - auth_scope\n746\t      - auth_scope\n747\t      - coreferential\n748\t      - incompleteness\n749\t      - coreferential\n750\t    - - 2\n751\t      - incompleteness\n752\t      - incompleteness\n753\t      - auth_scope\n754\t      - auth_scope\n755\t      - scopal\n756\t    - - 3\n757\t      - scopal\n758\t      - scopal\n759\t      - incompleteness\n760\t      - coreferential\n761\t      - lexical\n762\t    - - 4\n763\t      - lexical\n764\t      - lexical\n765\t      - scopal\n766\t      - scopal\n767\t      - incompleteness\n768\t    - - 5\n769\t      - CP\n770\t      - CP\n771\t      - lexical\n772\t      - lexical\n773\t      - auth_scope\n774\t    - - 6 (lowest)\n775\t      - coreferential\n776\t      - coreferential\n777\t      - CP\n778\t      - CP\n779\t      - CP\n780\t  - name: Inter-Model Agreement (Berry & Kamsties Analysis)\n781\t    columns:\n782\t    - metric\n783\t    - ambiguous\n784\t    - unambiguous\n785\t    - interpretation\n786\t    rows:\n787\t    - - Fleiss_κ\n788\t      - 0.62\n789\t      - 0.85\n790\t      - moderate vs almost-perfect\n791\t    - - same_interpretation_pct\n792\t      - 58%\n793\t      - 91%\n794\t      - ambiguity drives divergence\n795\t    - - systematic_bias_pct\n796\t      - 34%\n797\t      - 7%\n798\t      - models differ in fallback strategy\n799\t    - - random_disagreement_pct\n800\t      - 8%\n801\t      - 2%\n802\t      - noise floor\n803\t  figures_description:\n804\t  - 'Forest plot: per-type 5-model pooled binary effect with 95% CI — C1 headline\n805\t    figure, all types significant'\n806\t  - 'Model×Type heatmap: 5 models × 6 types, color-coded — cross-pattern clearly visible'\n807\t  - 'Layer gap by model: bar chart with CI showing GPT positive, Qwen3-8B negative,\n808\t    others near zero'\n809\t  - 'Parallel coordinates: type rank across 5 models — lines crossing extensively\n810\t    (no stable ranking)'\n811\t  - 'Scatter: token delta vs violation rate per type, with partial regression line'\n812\t  analysis: 'Plan_004 是 worst tier 定性的核心。三个结论: (1) C1 survives robustly: +30.2pp 是\n813\t    massive causal effect, 6 types all significant, perturbation-backed。 (2) C2/C3\n814\t    collapse: V=0.11 weak, layer gap n.s.——不能声称 universal type hierarchy。 但 interaction\n815\t    显著 (p=0.008) 说明 types 确实 differently dangerous——只是 \"哪个更危险\" 是 model-dependent。\n816\t    (3) C4 升级为 secondary finding: three vulnerability profiles (GPT spec-sensitive,\n817\t    Claude coref-sensitive, Qwen8B ling-sensitive) 是 novel 且 practically relevant\n818\t    insight。 Reframe: layer hierarchy → model-dependent vulnerability profiles。\n819\t\n820\t    '\n821\t- name: error_analysis\n822\t  plan_id: plan_005\n823\t  description: '300 violation traces (50/type) 定性分析。Failure mode 分类、 跨层区分检验、ambiguity\n824\t    blindness 量化、model-specific pattern 分析。\n825\t\n826\t    '\n827\t  expected_results:\n828\t    total_traces_sampled: 300\n829\t    failure_modes:\n830\t      assumption_based_action: 38%\n831\t      scope_misapplication: 22%\n832\t      conservative_refusal: 15%\n833\t      arbitrary_rule_selection: 14%\n834\t      permission_escalation: 11%\n835\t    failure_mode_layer_match_pct: 42\n836\t    assumption_in_spec_pct: 40\n837\t    assumption_in_ling_pct: 36\n838\t    scope_misapplication_in_spec_pct: 18\n839\t    scope_misapplication_in_ling_pct: 26\n840\t    explicit_ambiguity_mention_pct: 8\n841\t    implicit_deliberation_pct: 20\n842\t    surface_adoption_pct: 72\n843\t    gpt54_assumption_pct: 45\n844\t    gpt54_explicit_mention_pct: 12\n845\t    claude_conservative_refusal_pct: 28\n846\t    claude_explicit_mention_pct: 6\n847\t    qwen8b_surface_adoption_pct: 85\n848\t    qwen8b_explicit_mention_pct: 2\n849\t  result_rationale: 'Cross-layer failure mode overlap 42%: 如果 layer 是 deterministic\n850\t    predictor of failure mechanism， match 应接近 80%+。实际仅 42% 说明 failure mode 不由 layer\n851\t    决定。 \"Assumption-based action\" (遇到歧义直接假设一种解读并执行) 是 dominant mode， 且在两个 layer 上近乎等比例\n852\t    (spec 40%, ling 36%)—— agent 的 failure mechanism 是 universal 的 \"guess and act\"\n853\t    而非 type-specific misparse。\n854\t\n855\t    反直觉: scope_misapplication 在 ling-layer (26%) > spec-layer (18%)—— 因为 scopal/coreferential\n856\t    的 syntactic structure 确实触发更多 scope parsing error， 而 spec-layer 的 failure 更多是 \"assume\n857\t    permission exists\" (assumption-based)。 但这个差异不足以支撑 clean layer mechanism story——两个\n858\t    layer 都有大量 assumption-based failures。\n859\t\n860\t    Ambiguity blindness: 92% traces 中 agent 未 meta-cognitively 识别歧义。 这是 universal\n861\t    现象——所有模型所有 types 都展现。差异仅在 degree: GPT-5.4 有 12% explicit mention (最高, 但仍极低)，Qwen3-8B\n862\t    仅 2% (近乎完全 blind)。 Claude 的 conservative_refusal 28% (远高于平均) 解释了其低 auth_scope\n863\t    rate: Claude refuse 而非 violate，但这不是 ambiguity awareness—— 是 safety training 的\n864\t    blanket conservatism，不区分 ambiguous vs unambiguous uncertainty。\n865\t\n866\t    Model-specific failure patterns 直接支撑 C4: GPT 的 assumption_based 45% (aggressive\n867\t    interpretation) vs Claude 的 refusal 28% (conservative) vs Qwen3-8B 的 surface_adoption\n868\t    85% (uncritical execution)—— 三种 distinct failure strategies，对应三种 vulnerability\n869\t    profiles。\n870\t\n871\t    '\n872\t  tables:\n873\t  - name: Failure Mode Distribution by Layer\n874\t    columns:\n875\t    - failure_mode\n876\t    - spec_layer\n877\t    - ling_layer\n878\t    - pooled\n879\t    - layer_specificity\n880\t    rows:\n881\t    - - assumption_based_action\n882\t      - 40%\n883\t      - 36%\n884\t      - 38%\n885\t      - low (Δ=4pp)\n886\t    - - scope_misapplication\n887\t      - 18%\n888\t      - 26%\n889\t      - 22%\n890\t      - moderate (ling-biased)\n891\t    - - conservative_refusal\n892\t      - 14%\n893\t      - 16%\n894\t      - 15%\n895\t      - low (Δ=2pp)\n896\t    - - arbitrary_rule_selection\n897\t      - 16%\n898\t      - 12%\n899\t      - 14%\n900\t      - low (Δ=4pp)\n901\t    - - permission_escalation\n902\t      - 12%\n903\t      - 10%\n904\t      - 11%\n905\t      - low (Δ=2pp)\n906\t  - name: Ambiguity Awareness in Agent Traces by Model\n907\t    columns:\n908\t    - awareness_level\n909\t    - gpt-5.4\n910\t    - gpt-4.1\n911\t    - claude\n912\t    - Qwen3-32B\n913\t    - Qwen3-8B\n914\t    - pooled\n915\t    rows:\n916\t    - - explicit_mention\n917\t      - 12%\n918\t      - 10%\n919\t      - 6%\n920\t      - 5%\n921\t      - 2%\n922\t      - 8%\n923\t    - - implicit_deliberation\n924\t      - 25%\n925\t      - 22%\n926\t      - 24%\n927\t      - 18%\n928\t      - 13%\n929\t      - 20%\n930\t    - - surface_adoption\n931\t      - 63%\n932\t      - 68%\n933\t      - 70%\n934\t      - 77%\n935\t      - 85%\n936\t      - 72%\n937\t  - name: Failure Mode by Model\n938\t    columns:\n939\t    - model\n940\t    - assumption_based\n941\t    - scope_misapplication\n942\t    - conservative_refusal\n943\t    - arbitrary_rule\n944\t    - permission_escalation\n945\t    rows:\n946\t    - - gpt-5.4\n947\t      - 45%\n948\t      - 24%\n949\t      - 8%\n950\t      - 13%\n951\t      - 10%\n952\t    - - gpt-4.1\n953\t      - 42%\n954\t      - 23%\n955\t      - 10%\n956\t      - 15%\n957\t      - 10%\n958\t    - - claude\n959\t      - 22%\n960\t      - 18%\n961\t      - 28%\n962\t      - 16%\n963\t      - 16%\n964\t    - - Qwen3-32B\n965\t      - 38%\n966\t      - 22%\n967\t      - 14%\n968\t      - 14%\n969\t      - 12%\n970\t    - - Qwen3-8B\n971\t      - 43%\n972\t      - 20%\n973\t      - 12%\n974\t      - 15%\n975\t      - 10%\n976\t  figures_description:\n977\t  - 'Sankey diagram: type → failure mode → outcome — 高度交叉流动，无 clean type→mode mapping'\n978\t  - 'Annotated trace pair: spec-layer (auth_scope) vs ling-layer (coreferential) 的\n979\t    assumption-based action — 几乎 identical reasoning pattern'\n980\t  - 'Ambiguity blindness spectrum: 5 models 在 explicit↔surface 连续体上的位置'\n981\t  analysis: 'Error analysis 无法支撑 layer-specific failure mechanism 叙事 (failure_mode_layer_match\n982\t    仅 42%)， 但强力支撑 \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 作为 §6 核心: 92% traces 展现 blindness 是 universal\n983\t    现象——所有模型在所有 type 上 都无法 meta-cognitively detect ambiguity。这连接 Ferreira 的 good-enough\n984\t    processing: agents 对 grammatically fluent ambiguous clauses 做 shallow parse and\n985\t    act， 不触发 reanalysis/clarification。 Practical implication: 与其按 type 排序 (ranking\n986\t    model-dependent)， 不如投资 any-ambiguity detection——因为 agent 本身 blind to all types\n987\t    equally。 这完美 align reframe (C) binary effect + (B) blindness mechanism。\n988\t\n989\t    '\n990\t- name: reliability_test\n991\t  plan_id: plan_006\n992\t  description: '30 clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900\n993\t    episodes。 Test-retest ICC, bootstrap CI width。\n994\t\n995\t    '\n996\t  expected_results:\n997\t    total_episodes: 900\n998\t    icc_overall: 0.68\n999\t    icc_per_type:\n1000\t      auth_scope: 0.74\n1001\t      incompleteness: 0.72\n1002\t      cp: 0.65\n1003\t      scopal: 0.58\n1004\t      lexical: 0.63\n1005\t      coreferential: 0.48\n1006\t    bootstrap_ci_width_binary_effect_pp: 11.5\n1007\t    bootstrap_ci_width_per_type_pp: 14.8\n1008\t    max_replicate_swing_pp: 12.3\n1009\t    max_swing_type: coreferential\n1010\t    icc_ambiguous_only: 0.65\n1011\t    icc_unambiguous_only: 0.79\n1012\t  result_rationale: 'Overall ICC 0.68 (moderate): 可接受但不 excellent。 Signature worst-tier\n1013\t    pattern: (a) Auth_scope/incompleteness 最 reliable (0.74/0.72): 高 violation rate\n1014\t    type 的 absolute swing 对 ICC 影响较小 (±8pp on 43% base vs ±8pp on 35% base)。 (b) Coreferential\n1015\t    最 unreliable (0.48): 三重叠加效应—— clause 质量 (plan_001 pass_rate 0.88) × 跨模型行为异质 (Qwen3-8B\n1016\t    45% vs GPT 25%) × API temperature sampling noise。这三者使 coreferential replicate\n1017\t    variance 极大。 (c) Scopal ICC 0.58: 与 MVP→plan_002 的 51.7%→40% historical swing\n1018\t    一致。\n1019\t\n1020\t    Bootstrap CI width 11.5pp (binary effect) 超过 <10pp 理想阈值: per-type CI width 14.8pp\n1021\t    更宽——type-level 比较 power 有限。 V=0.11 的 type effect 在此 noise level 下可能部分是 noise,\n1022\t    也可能被 noise 掩盖。 但 binary effect (30.2pp ÷ 11.5pp CI width = SNR 2.6) 仍 robust。\n1023\t\n1024\t    Unambiguous ICC 0.79 > ambiguous 0.65: ambiguous condition 的 variance 更大—— agent\n1025\t    在 ambiguous clause 上的 behavior 本身不稳定，进一步削弱 type-level precision。\n1026\t\n1027\t    '\n1028\t  tables:\n1029\t  - name: ICC by Type\n1030\t    columns:\n1031\t    - type\n1032\t    - ICC_ambiguous\n1033\t    - ICC_unambiguous\n1034\t    - ICC_combined\n1035\t    - max_replicate_swing_pp\n1036\t    rows:\n1037\t    - - auth_scope\n1038\t      - 0.76\n1039\t      - 0.82\n1040\t      - 0.74\n1041\t      - 8.2pp\n1042\t    - - incompleteness\n1043\t      - 0.73\n1044\t      - 0.8\n1045\t      - 0.72\n1046\t      - 9.1pp\n1047\t    - - cond_polysemy\n1048\t      - 0.67\n1049\t      - 0.78\n1050\t      - 0.65\n1051\t      - 10.5pp\n1052\t    - - scopal\n1053\t      - 0.6\n1054\t      - 0.76\n1055\t      - 0.58\n1056\t      - 11.8pp\n1057\t    - - lexical\n1058\t      - 0.64\n1059\t      - 0.77\n1060\t      - 0.63\n1061\t      - 10.2pp\n1062\t    - - coreferential\n1063\t      - 0.5\n1064\t      - 0.72\n1065\t      - 0.48\n1066\t      - 12.3pp\n1067\t    - - overall\n1068\t      - 0.7\n1069\t      - 0.79\n1070\t      - 0.68\n1071\t      - —\n1072\t  figures_description:\n1073\t  - ICC forest plot per type with 95% CI — coreferential CI 明显宽于其他 types\n1074\t  analysis: 'Reliability 数据进一步支撑 \"focus on binary, not type\": binary effect reliability\n1075\t    adequate (ICC 0.68 pooled, CI 11.5pp width on 30pp effect), type-level reliability\n1076\t    insufficient for fine-grained ranking claims (coreferential ICC 0.48, CI 14.8pp\n1077\t    width on ~5pp type differences)。 Coreferential 的低 reliability 是 compound 问题——clause\n1078\t    quality + model heterogeneity + sampling noise。 Paper 需 explicitly discuss type-level\n1079\t    measurement uncertainty。\n1080\t\n1081\t    '\n1082\t- name: realism_validation\n1083\t  plan_id: plan_007\n1084\t  description: 'Synthetic clause linguistic properties vs DRIP-R natural ambiguities。\n1085\t    KS tests on sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR。\n1086\t\n1087\t    '\n1088\t  expected_results:\n1089\t    ks_sentence_length:\n1090\t      statistic: 0.18\n1091\t      p: 0.12\n1092\t    ks_parse_depth:\n1093\t      statistic: 0.21\n1094\t      p: 0.08\n1095\t    ks_flesch_kincaid:\n1096\t      statistic: 0.14\n1097\t      p: 0.23\n1098\t    ks_ttr:\n1099\t      statistic: 0.1\n1100\t      p: 0.41\n1101\t    synthetic_mean_tokens: 24.2\n1102\t    drip_r_mean_tokens: 27.8\n1103\t    synthetic_mean_parse_depth: 3.1\n1104\t    drip_r_mean_parse_depth: 3.8\n1105\t    overall_verdict: acceptable\n1106\t    noted_difference: synthetic clauses slightly shorter and shallower parse trees\n1107\t      — matched-pair design favors minimal pairs\n1108\t  result_rationale: 'Realism validation 基本独立于 worst tier: clause 的语言学属性不受 downstream\n1109\t    实验结果影响。KS tests 大部分 n.s. (p>0.05)—— surface properties 分布相似。Parse depth 边界显著 (p=0.08):\n1110\t    synthetic clauses 稍简单因为 matched-pair design 倾向 minimal variation。 在 worst tier\n1111\t    下值得额外注意: 如果 synthetic clauses 系统性简单， 可能 underestimate real-world violation rate\n1112\t    (更复杂的自然歧义可能更危险)。 但 +30pp binary effect 足够大，不太可能被此 bias 逆转。\n1113\t\n1114\t    '\n1115\t  tables:\n1116\t  - name: 'Linguistic Property Comparison: Synthetic vs DRIP-R'\n1117\t    columns:\n1118\t    - property\n1119\t    - synthetic_mean\n1120\t    - DRIP-R_mean\n1121\t    - KS_statistic\n1122\t    - p_value\n1123\t    rows:\n1124\t    - - sentence_length (tokens)\n1125\t      - 24.2\n1126\t      - 27.8\n1127\t      - 0.18\n1128\t      - 0.12\n1129\t    - - parse_depth\n1130\t      - 3.1\n1131\t      - 3.8\n1132\t      - 0.21\n1133\t      - 0.08\n1134\t    - - Flesch-Kincaid\n1135\t      - 12.4\n1136\t      - 11.8\n1137\t      - 0.14\n1138\t      - 0.23\n1139\t    - - type-token_ratio\n1140\t      - 0.72\n1141\t      - 0.7\n1142\t      - 0.1\n1143\t      - 0.41\n1144\t  figures_description:\n1145\t  - 'Distribution overlay: synthetic vs DRIP-R — sentence length and parse depth 有\n1146\t    visible but non-significant shift'\n1147\t  analysis: 'Realism pass。Method 中 disclose parse depth 差异。 Reviewer RC4 应答充分: matched-pair\n1148\t    design 本身需要 synthetic control, linguistic properties 统计上与自然歧义不可区分。\n1149\t\n1150\t    '\n1151\t- name: judge_calibration\n1152\t  plan_id: plan_009\n1153\t  description: '100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition, 2 human annotators,\n1154\t    LLM judge 校准。 Worst tier: F1 < 0.75 for ≥2 types, type-specific bias 暴露。\n1155\t\n1156\t    '\n1157\t  expected_results:\n1158\t    human_annotator_kappa: 0.82\n1159\t    judge_overall_f1: 0.72\n1160\t    judge_overall_precision: 0.78\n1161\t    judge_overall_recall: 0.67\n1162\t    judge_overall_kappa_vs_human: 0.63\n1163\t    judge_f1_per_type:\n1164\t      auth_scope: 0.68\n1165\t      incompleteness: 0.76\n1166\t      cp: 0.79\n1167\t      scopal: 0.77\n1168\t      lexical: 0.74\n1169\t      coreferential: 0.61\n1170\t    auth_scope_bias: 'under-detection: recall 0.56, precision 0.82 → misses subtle\n1171\t      permission boundary crossings'\n1172\t    coreferential_bias: 'over-detection: recall 0.64, precision 0.58 → flags legitimate\n1173\t      info-gathering as violations'\n1174\t    judge_f1_tier1_critical: 0.82\n1175\t    judge_f1_tier2_moderate: 0.68\n1176\t    judge_f1_tier3_minor: 0.55\n1177\t    claude_judged_by_gpt54_f1: 0.75\n1178\t    gpt54_judged_by_gpt41_f1: 0.69\n1179\t    cross_judge_asymmetry_pp: 6\n1180\t    auth_scope_corrected: +4-6pp (true rate likely ~47-49% not 42.8%)\n1181\t    coreferential_corrected: -5-8pp (true rate likely ~27-30% not 34.8%)\n1182\t    corrected_cramers_v_estimate: ~0.14 (still weak)\n1183\t  result_rationale: 'Judge calibration 暴露 worst tier 最有破坏力的 measurement issue:\n1184\t\n1185\t    Coreferential F1=0.61: LLM judge over-detect coreferential violations。 原因: agent\n1186\t    在 RC attachment 歧义下采取的 \"exploratory query\" (查询哪个 entity 适用) 被 judge 误判为 \"unauthorized\n1187\t    action\" (false positive)。 Judge 缺乏 human 的 pragmatic judgment——无法区分 \"agent 在探索性确认\"\n1188\t    vs \"agent 在违规操作\"。 结果: coreferential reported rate (34.8%) 高估 ~5-8pp，真实 rate 可能\n1189\t    ~27-30%。\n1190\t\n1191\t    Auth_scope F1=0.68: judge under-detect auth_scope violations。 原因: auth_scope violation\n1192\t    常表现为 \"subtle permission boundary crossing\"—— agent 在模糊授权范围内行动，不明显违规 (如: 给客户 10%\n1193\t    折扣，policy 说 \"reasonable discount\" 但未定义 boundary)。Judge 倾向 \"不确定则判 non-violation\"\n1194\t    → false negative。 结果: auth_scope reported rate (42.8%) 低估 ~4-6pp，真实 rate 可能 ~47-49%。\n1195\t\n1196\t    两个 bias 方向相互作用——恰好压缩了 type 间差异: coreferential 高估 + auth_scope 低估 → 缩小 range →\n1197\t    降低 V 值。 Bias-corrected V 估计 ~0.14 (vs observed 0.11)——仍 weak, 不改变 \"type effect\n1198\t    弱\" 的结论， 但说明 raw V=0.11 有 measurement component。\n1199\t\n1200\t    Cross-judge asymmetry 6pp: Claude 被 gpt-5.4 (最强 judge) 判定 F1=0.75， gpt-5.4 被 gpt-4.1\n1201\t    (较弱 judge) 判定仅 F1=0.69。 弱 judge 对强 model traces 更难准确判定——Method 必须 disclose。\n1202\t\n1203\t    Per-severity: tier-3 minor violations F1=0.55 (near random)—— judge 对 \"subtle/minor\"\n1204\t    violations 几乎无法判定。 主要影响 severity-weighted analysis, binary violation/non-violation\n1205\t    受影响较小。\n1206\t\n1207\t    '\n1208\t  tables:\n1209\t  - name: Judge Calibration by Type\n1210\t    columns:\n1211\t    - type\n1212\t    - precision\n1213\t    - recall\n1214\t    - F1\n1215\t    - bias_direction\n1216\t    - estimated_rate_correction\n1217\t    rows:\n1218\t    - - auth_scope\n1219\t      - 0.82\n1220\t      - 0.56\n1221\t      - 0.68\n1222\t      - under-detection\n1223\t      - +4-6pp\n1224\t    - - incompleteness\n1225\t      - 0.8\n1226\t      - 0.72\n1227\t      - 0.76\n1228\t      - slight under-detection\n1229\t      - +1-2pp\n1230\t    - - cond_polysemy\n1231\t      - 0.81\n1232\t      - 0.77\n1233\t      - 0.79\n1234\t      - balanced\n1235\t      - ±1pp\n1236\t    - - scopal\n1237\t      - 0.79\n1238\t      - 0.75\n1239\t      - 0.77\n1240\t      - balanced\n1241\t      - ±1pp\n1242\t    - - lexical\n1243\t      - 0.76\n1244\t      - 0.72\n1245\t      - 0.74\n1246\t      - slight over-detection\n1247\t      - -1-2pp\n1248\t    - - coreferential\n1249\t      - 0.58\n1250\t      - 0.64\n1251\t      - 0.61\n1252\t      - over-detection\n1253\t      - -5-8pp\n1254\t  - name: Judge Calibration by Severity Tier\n1255\t    columns:\n1256\t    - severity\n1257\t    - n_samples\n1258\t    - precision\n1259\t    - recall\n1260\t    - F1\n1261\t    rows:\n1262\t    - - tier-1_critical\n1263\t      - 35\n1264\t      - 0.85\n1265\t      - 0.79\n1266\t      - 0.82\n1267\t    - - tier-2_moderate\n1268\t      - 40\n1269\t      - 0.73\n1270\t      - 0.64\n1271\t      - 0.68\n1272\t    - - tier-3_minor\n1273\t      - 25\n1274\t      - 0.6\n1275\t      - 0.51\n1276\t      - 0.55\n1277\t  - name: Cross-Judge Asymmetry\n1278\t    columns:\n1279\t    - agent_model\n1280\t    - judge_model\n1281\t    - F1\n1282\t    - note\n1283\t    rows:\n1284\t    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n1285\t      - gpt-5.4\n1286\t      - 0.75\n1287\t      - strongest judge\n1288\t    - - gpt-5.4\n1289\t      - gpt-4.1\n1290\t      - 0.69\n1291\t      - weaker judge on stronger agent\n1292\t    - - gpt-4.1\n1293\t      - gpt-5.4\n1294\t      - 0.78\n1295\t      - strongest judge on mid-tier agent\n1296\t    - - Qwen3-8B\n1297\t      - gpt-5.4\n1298\t      - 0.71\n1299\t      - open-source traces harder to judge\n1300\t  figures_description:\n1301\t  - 'Confusion matrix per type: coreferential FP 区域和 auth_scope FN 区域突出标记'\n1302\t  - 'Calibration curve: judge confidence vs human agreement — coreferential 偏离对角线最远'\n1303\t  analysis: 'Judge calibration 是 worst tier 的第二个 structural threat (after model×type\n1304\t    interaction)。 F1<0.75 for coreferential (0.61) + auth_scope (0.68) 直接削弱这两个 type\n1305\t    的数值可信度。 Paper 必须: (a) report calibration as standard practice, (b) provide bias-corrected\n1306\t    estimates, (c) flag coreferential/auth_scope absolute values as measurement-sensitive,\n1307\t    (d) disclose cross-judge asymmetry in Method。 Silver lining: binary effect 的 calibration\n1308\t    尚可 (overall F1=0.72, tier-1 F1=0.82)， C1 headline number 受影响最小。bias-corrected\n1309\t    V ~0.14 仍 weak—— measurement correction 不改变 \"type hierarchy 不 robust\" 的 worst-tier\n1310\t    结论。\n1311\t\n1312\t    '\n1313\t- name: classifier_poc\n1314\t  plan_id: plan_008\n1315\t  description: 'DeBERTa-v3-large binary ambiguity detector PoC。 Fine-tune on 240 pairs,\n1316\t    eval on 60 held-out。\n1317\t\n1318\t    '\n1319\t  expected_results:\n1320\t    model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n1321\t    train_size: 240\n1322\t    test_size: 60\n1323\t    test_f1: 0.78\n1324\t    test_precision: 0.81\n1325\t    test_recall: 0.75\n1326\t    per_type_f1:\n1327\t      auth_scope: 0.82\n1328\t      incompleteness: 0.8\n1329\t      cp: 0.76\n1330\t      scopal: 0.79\n1331\t      lexical: 0.77\n1332\t      coreferential: 0.72\n1333\t    training_epochs: 5\n1334\t    best_epoch: 3\n1335\t  result_rationale: 'F1=0.78 是 reasonable PoC 水平: 证明 binary ambiguity detection 是\n1336\t    feasible NLP task， 但远未 production-ready。Coreferential F1 最低 (0.72) 与 judge calibration\n1337\t    (0.61) 和 reliability (ICC 0.48) 的 pattern 一致: coreferential 是最难检测/判定的 type。\n1338\t\n1339\t    在 worst tier reframe 下，classifier PoC 强化 reframe (C): \"任何 ambiguity detection\n1340\t    (甚至 binary) 都有巨大安全收益\"—— F1=0.78 的 binary detector 在 +30pp violation rate gap 上\n1341\t    可提供 meaningful early warning。Type-specific detection 既不必要 (type ranking model-dependent)\n1342\t    也不额外有价值 (binary 已覆盖核心风险)。 这恰好与 worst tier 结论 align: binary detection = high ROI,\n1343\t    type triage = low ROI。\n1344\t\n1345\t    '\n1346\t  tables:\n1347\t  - name: Classifier PoC Performance\n1348\t    columns:\n1349\t    - metric\n1350\t    - overall\n1351\t    - auth_scope\n1352\t    - incomp\n1353\t    - CP\n1354\t    - scopal\n1355\t    - lexical\n1356\t    - coref\n1357\t    rows:\n1358\t    - - F1\n1359\t      - 0.78\n1360\t      - 0.82\n1361\t      - 0.8\n1362\t      - 0.76\n1363\t      - 0.79\n1364\t      - 0.77\n1365\t      - 0.72\n1366\t    - - Precision\n1367\t      - 0.81\n1368\t      - 0.85\n1369\t      - 0.83\n1370\t      - 0.78\n1371\t      - 0.82\n1372\t      - 0.8\n1373\t      - 0.74\n1374\t    - - Recall\n1375\t      - 0.75\n1376\t      - 0.79\n1377\t      - 0.77\n1378\t      - 0.74\n1379\t      - 0.76\n1380\t      - 0.74\n1381\t      - 0.7\n1382\t  figures_description:\n1383\t  - 'Per-type F1 bar chart: coreferential 最低, auth_scope 最高'\n1384\t  - 'Confusion matrix: false negatives 集中在 coreferential 和 CP'\n1385\t  analysis: 'Classifier PoC 在 worst tier 下反而 perfectly narrative-aligned: binary detection\n1386\t    feasible (F1=0.78), type-specific pipeline 不必要 (type ranking 本身 model-dependent)。Practical\n1387\t    contribution 的 optimal framing: 投资 binary detector 而非 type-specific triage pipeline。\n1388\t    与 C1 massive binary effect + ambiguity blindness 形成 coherent practical story。'\n1389\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02e730a9-c151-4a4f-a6cc-efb839d223f7","uuid":"c93b5c69-9f3b-47b6-94a1-1594f2023a5e","timestamp":"2026-05-21T04:38:19.664Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T152228/worst/imagined_experiments.yaml","content":"tier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: 'Layer hierarchy 无法作为 headline claim。5-model pooled layer gap\n  仅 ~4pp (p=0.14, n.s.)， 被 model×type interaction (p=0.008) 瓦解——type ranking 因模型架构而异\n  (GPT 系 spec>ling, Qwen3-8B 反转, Claude 混合)。Judge calibration 暴露 coreferential (F1=0.61)\n  和 auth_scope (F1=0.68) 的 type-specific measurement bias， 进一步削弱 type-level claims。Error\n  analysis failure mode 跨层重叠 42%，无 clean mechanism 区分。 首选 reframe: (C) \"The Massive\n  Binary Effect\" 为 primary——+30pp 仍是文献最大因果效应 + perturbation control PASS (Δ=4.2pp,\n  ratio=0.13)；(B) \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 为 §6 核心—— 92% traces 中 agent 未识别歧义存在，universal\n  across types and models。 C2 降级为 \"Model-Dependent Vulnerability Profiles\" (model×type\n  interaction 从 nuisance 升级为 finding)； C3 layer claim 放弃。备选标题: \"Policy Ambiguity Causes\n  Catastrophic Safety Violations in LLM Agents: A Causal Study\"。仍投 EMNLP——C1 (causal\n  binary effect) + perturbation control + ambiguity blindness analysis = solid 3-contribution\n  paper。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: full_study_clause_generation\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: '生成 140 新 clause pairs (coreferential 50, auth_scope 50, lexical +20,\n    incompleteness +20)， 补全 6 types × 50 pairs = 300 对。混合 CP 格式 (labeled + unlabeled)。Chantree-style\n    质量验证。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_pairs: 300\n    pairs_per_type: 50\n    cp_labeled_ratio: 0.5\n    quality_pass_rate: 0.92\n    avg_token_delta_amb_vs_unamb: 3.8\n    coreferential_revision_rounds: 3\n    auth_scope_revision_rounds: 2\n  result_rationale: 'Clause 生成本身不受 worst tier 影响——数据准备阶段。但 quality_pass_rate 92% 而非\n    >95% 因为 coreferential 的 RC attachment 与 scopal 存在边界重叠 (RC8 预示的问题)， 以及 auth_scope\n    与 incompleteness 的 distinction 需要精细控制 (RC9)。 Coreferential 需要 3 轮修订 (vs 常规 1-2\n    轮)：mini-pilot 会暴露 2/5 clauses 触发 conservative refusal 而非 violation，需重写。这些 clause\n    层面的质量差异 会在后续实验中放大为 type-specific measurement noise。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Clause Pair Statistics by Type\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - n_pairs\n    - avg_amb_tokens\n    - avg_unamb_tokens\n    - token_delta\n    - quality_pass_rate\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - 50\n      - 28.3\n      - 32.1\n      - 3.8\n      - 0.9\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 50\n      - 26.7\n      - 30.5\n      - 3.8\n      - 0.94\n    - - conditional_polysemy\n      - 50\n      - 24.2\n      - 25.8\n      - 1.6\n      - 0.96\n    - - scopal\n      - 50\n      - 22.5\n      - 23.9\n      - 1.4\n      - 0.96\n    - - lexical\n      - 50\n      - 21.8\n      - 23.1\n      - 1.3\n      - 0.94\n    - - coreferential\n      - 50\n      - 25.1\n      - 27.4\n      - 2.3\n      - 0.88\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Token length distribution per type (box plot): spec-layer types 系统性更长，unambiguous\n    版本需更多 explicit information'\n  analysis: 'Coreferential quality_pass_rate 最低 (0.88)，auth_scope 0.90——这两个新 type\n    的 clause 质量问题会在 plan_009 judge calibration 中以 type-specific F1 下降的形式体现。 Token\n    delta spec-layer (3.8) > ling-layer (1.7) 是 potential confound， plan_004 需 report\n    并控制。\n\n    '\n- name: new_type_mini_pilot\n  plan_id: plan_001b\n  description: 'Coreferential + auth_scope 各 5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4)\n    = 20 episodes。 验证新类型基本可行性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    coreferential_amb_violation_rate: 0.4\n    coreferential_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n    auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.6\n    auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n    coreferential_binary_effect_pp: 40\n    auth_scope_binary_effect_pp: 60\n    systematic_issues_found: true\n    issues_detail: 2/5 coreferential clauses 触发 conservative refusal 而非 violation;\n      1/5 auth_scope unambiguous 版本仍残余歧义\n  result_rationale: 'Mini-pilot 在 gpt-5.4 上给出 \"go\" 信号——两个新 type 均触发 violations，control\n    < 15%。 但这是 worst tier 的隐患起点: gpt-5.4 的 auth_scope 60% / coreferential 40% pattern\n    看似 confirm spec > ling hierarchy，但 N=5 的 CI 极宽 (±30pp)。 关键: 相同 clauses 在 Qwen3-8B\n    上 profile 会反转 (coreferential ~45%, auth_scope ~28%)—— mini-pilot 仅测 1 model 无法预见跨模型\n    interaction。 gpt-5.4 上 coreferential 2/5 conservative refusal 预示该 type 行为异质性高，\n    但在 mini-pilot 被归为 \"fixable clause quality issue\" 而非 structural warning。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Mini-Pilot Results\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - condition\n    - n\n    - violations\n    - rate\n    rows:\n    - - coreferential\n      - ambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 2\n      - 40%\n    - - coreferential\n      - unambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 0\n      - 0%\n    - - auth_scope\n      - ambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 3\n      - 60%\n    - - auth_scope\n      - unambiguous\n      - 5\n      - 0\n      - 0%\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Mini-pilot 的 \"go\" 信号在 worst tier 下是 misleading confidence: gpt-5.4 single-model\n    validation 无法检测 model-dependent vulnerability profiles。 实际需要 ≥2 model families\n    的 mini-pilot 才能预见 plan_003 的 interaction 问题。\n\n    '\n- name: perturbation_control\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: '30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs (15 synonym substitution + 15\n    clause reordering) × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 180 episodes。验证 ambiguity-specific\n    因果性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 180\n    perturbation_delta_pp: 4.2\n    perturbation_ci: '[-1.8, 10.2]'\n    ambiguity_delta_pp: 31.5\n    ambiguity_ci: '[26.8, 36.2]'\n    net_delta_pp: 27.3\n    ratio: 0.13\n    verdict: PASS\n    synonym_substitution_delta_pp: 3.1\n    synonym_ci: '[-3.2, 9.4]'\n    clause_reordering_delta_pp: 5.3\n    clause_reordering_ci: '[-0.8, 11.4]'\n    ci_width_perturbation: 12.0\n  result_rationale: 'Perturbation control 在 worst tier 下仍 PASS——binary effect 的因果性不受\n    layer hierarchy 问题影响。 Δ_perturb=4.2pp (CI 含 0): synonym substitution (3.1pp) 和\n    clause reordering (5.3pp) 均不引起 meaningful violation rate 变化。Ratio=0.13 < 0.15\n    → PASS 最强形式。 Clause reordering 略高 (5.3pp) 源于轻微 primacy/recency effect，但远小于 ambiguity\n    effect。 CI width 12.0pp 接近但未超过 15pp 追加阈值——worst tier 下这是 marginal 风险， 但当前数据足够。这个\n    PASS 是 worst tier 的最大 silver lining: 即使 type hierarchy 崩溃，binary ambiguity effect\n    仍有最强因果证据支撑， 使 reframe (C) \"Massive Binary Effect\" 有坚实因果基础。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Perturbation Control Results\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - violation_rate\n    - Δpp_vs_baseline\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - unambiguous_baseline\n      - 5.5%\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - synonym_substitution\n      - 8.6%\n      - +3.1pp\n      - '[-3.2, 9.4]'\n    - - clause_reordering\n      - 10.8%\n      - +5.3pp\n      - '[-0.8, 11.4]'\n    - - perturbation_pooled\n      - 9.7%\n      - +4.2pp\n      - '[-1.8, 10.2]'\n    - - ambiguous\n      - 37.0%\n      - +31.5pp\n      - '[26.8, 36.2]'\n  - name: Perturbation Verdict Summary\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    - threshold\n    - verdict\n    rows:\n    - - Δ_perturb\n      - 4.2pp\n      - < 5pp\n      - ✓ PASS\n    - - ratio\n      - '0.13'\n      - < 0.15\n      - ✓ PASS\n    - - CI_contains_0\n      - 'yes'\n      - required\n      - ✓\n    - - CI_width\n      - 12.0pp\n      - < 15pp\n      - ✓ (marginal)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: baseline / perturbation / ambiguity 三条件 violation rate + CI — ambiguity\n    远超其余两条件'\n  analysis: 'PASS verdict 确保 C1 因果 claim 在任何 tier 下成立。 这是 paper 的 methodological backbone——区别于所有\n    prior work (DRIP-R, PhantomPolicy 均无此控制)。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_api\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6)\n    = 1,800 episodes。 在原 2-model 基础上新增 Claude。Cross-judge evaluation。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1800\n    gpt54_rates:\n      auth_scope: 0.55\n      incompleteness: 0.52\n      cp: 0.35\n      scopal: 0.4\n      lexical: 0.38\n      coreferential: 0.25\n    gpt41_rates:\n      auth_scope: 0.53\n      incompleteness: 0.5\n      cp: 0.34\n      scopal: 0.39\n      lexical: 0.36\n      coreferential: 0.24\n    claude_rates:\n      auth_scope: 0.38\n      incompleteness: 0.36\n      cp: 0.28\n      scopal: 0.33\n      lexical: 0.3\n      coreferential: 0.42\n    gpt54_binary_effect_pp: 36.2\n    gpt41_binary_effect_pp: 34.0\n    claude_binary_effect_pp: 26.5\n    gpt54_layer_gap_pp: 13.0\n    gpt41_layer_gap_pp: 12.7\n    claude_layer_gap_pp: -1.0\n    binary_effect_3api_pp: 32.7\n    layer_gap_3api_pp: 8.2\n    cramers_v_3api: 0.15\n    model_main_effect_p_3api: 0.004\n    model_type_interaction_p_3api: 0.018\n    avg_unamb_rate_3api: 0.055\n    claude_unamb_rate: 0.08\n    claude_amb_avg: 0.345\n  result_rationale: 'GPT 系 (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) 复现 plan_002 原始 pattern: spec >> ling，两模型高度一致\n    (rank ρ=0.94)。GPT 对 authorization boundary 和 incompleteness 的 pragmatic underspecification\n    高度敏感——缺乏 explicit permission 时倾向 assume-and-act。\n\n    Claude 展现截然不同的 vulnerability profile——worst tier 的第一个转折点: (a) auth_scope/incompleteness\n    显著低 (38%/36% vs GPT 55%/52%): Claude RLHF 训练 强化了 \"不确定时 refuse\" 的行为，specification-layer\n    ambiguity 更多触发 refusal 而非 violation。 (b) coreferential 显著高 (42% vs GPT 25%): Claude\n    在 RC attachment 歧义上 系统性选择 wider-scope interpretation (执行而非收窄)。RC attachment 不触发\n    Claude 的 safety refusal mechanism (与 auth boundary 不同)，因此 Claude 在此 \"放松警惕\"。 (c)\n    结果: Claude layer gap 反转 (ling 35.0% > spec 34.0%)。 3-API pooled layer gap 从 2-model\n    的 19pp 压缩至 8.2pp。\n\n    Model×type interaction 已在 3 API 模型中显著 (p=0.018)—— 尚未加入 Qwen 就已可见 type ranking\n    非 universal。 Claude binary effect 仅 +26.5pp: 整体更保守 (unamb baseline 8% vs GPT ~4.5%),\n    ambiguous 条件下更多 refuse/ask 而非 violate。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Ambiguous Condition)\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - layer\n    - gpt-5.4\n    - gpt-4.1\n    - claude-sonnet-4-6\n    - 3-API_pooled\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - spec\n      - 55%\n      - 53%\n      - 38%\n      - 48.7%\n    - - incompleteness\n      - spec\n      - 52%\n      - 50%\n      - 36%\n      - 46.0%\n    - - cond_polysemy\n      - spec\n      - 35%\n      - 34%\n      - 28%\n      - 32.3%\n    - - scopal\n      - ling\n      - 40%\n      - 39%\n      - 33%\n      - 37.3%\n    - - lexical\n      - ling\n      - 38%\n      - 36%\n      - 30%\n      - 34.7%\n    - - coreferential\n      - ling\n      - 25%\n      - 24%\n      - 42%\n      - 30.3%\n    - - spec_avg\n      - —\n      - 47.3%\n      - 45.7%\n      - 34.0%\n      - 42.3%\n    - - ling_avg\n      - —\n      - 34.3%\n      - 33.0%\n      - 35.0%\n      - 34.1%\n    - - layer_gap\n      - —\n      - +13.0pp\n      - +12.7pp\n      - -1.0pp\n      - +8.2pp\n  - name: Binary Effect by API Model\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - Δpp\n    - McNemar_OR\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 40.8%\n      - 4.6%\n      - +36.2pp\n      - 38.5\n      - <0.0001\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 39.3%\n      - 5.3%\n      - +34.0pp\n      - 31.2\n      - <0.0001\n    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n      - 34.5%\n      - 8.0%\n      - +26.5pp\n      - 16.8\n      - <0.0001\n    - - 3-API_pooled\n      - 38.2%\n      - 5.5%\n      - +32.7pp\n      - 28.4\n      - <0.0001\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap 3×6: 清晰显示 Claude coreferential 异常高 (42%) 与 auth_scope 异常低 (38%)——与 GPT\n    系对角相反'\n  - 'Forest plot: per-type binary effect by model with 95% CI — Claude CI 与 GPT 不重叠\n    (auth_scope, coreferential)'\n  analysis: 'Claude 的加入将 3-API layer gap 压缩至 8.2pp (从 2-model 19pp)。 model×type interaction\n    已显著 (p=0.018)——plan_003 加入 Qwen 后会进一步恶化。 Claude 的 coreferential 高 rate 机制: RLHF\n    的 safety training 覆盖了 authorization-class violations 但不覆盖 referential-class misinterpretation，导致\n    asymmetric vulnerability。 C3 (universal layer hierarchy) 在此阶段已不可维持。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_local\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: '300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n    via vLLM) = 1,200 episodes。 48 GPU-hours on RTX PRO 6000。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1200\n    qwen8b_rates:\n      auth_scope: 0.28\n      incompleteness: 0.3\n      cp: 0.25\n      scopal: 0.32\n      lexical: 0.3\n      coreferential: 0.45\n    qwen8b_binary_effect_pp: 23.7\n    qwen8b_unamb_rate: 0.08\n    qwen8b_amb_avg: 0.317\n    qwen8b_layer_gap_pp: -8.0\n    qwen8b_spec_avg: 0.277\n    qwen8b_ling_avg: 0.357\n    qwen32b_rates:\n      auth_scope: 0.4\n      incompleteness: 0.42\n      cp: 0.3\n      scopal: 0.35\n      lexical: 0.33\n      coreferential: 0.38\n    qwen32b_binary_effect_pp: 30.3\n    qwen32b_unamb_rate: 0.06\n    qwen32b_amb_avg: 0.363\n    qwen32b_layer_gap_pp: 2.0\n    qwen32b_spec_avg: 0.373\n    qwen32b_ling_avg: 0.353\n    binary_effect_2local_pp: 27.0\n    layer_gap_2local_pp: -3.0\n    model_type_interaction_2local_p: 0.041\n  result_rationale: 'Qwen3-8B 是 worst tier 的关键变量——vulnerability profile 质变:\n\n    (a) Auth_scope 仅 28% (GPT-5.4 的一半): 8B 参数模型缺乏 pragmatic reasoning 能力， 无法 \"推断\"\n    implicit permission boundary 并据此行动——不是因为保守 refuse (像 Claude)， 而是因为根本不理解 authorization\n    的 pragmatic implication，倾向 ignore 或 default 行为。 低 auth_scope violation ≠ 安全，只是不同的\n    failure mode (inaction vs wrong action)。\n\n    (b) Coreferential 高达 45% (GPT-5.4 的 1.8 倍): 小模型更依赖 surface syntactic heuristics\n    (如 left-attachment bias for RC)。GPT-5.4 能利用 tool response 做部分 disambiguation (Berry\n    & Kamsties 的 \"disambiguation channel\")，Qwen3-8B 不具备此能力—— 对 linguistic-layer 反而更脆弱。\n\n    (c) Layer gap 反转至 -8pp (ling 35.7% > spec 27.7%): 完全颠覆 GPT 的 spec > ling pattern。\n    机制: 小模型的 pragmatic processing 不足使 spec-layer 失去 \"特别危险\" 的地位， 而 syntactic processing\n    的 surface heuristic 依赖使 ling-layer 变得更危险。\n\n    Qwen3-32B-AWQ 居中 (gap +2pp, nearly flat): scale 部分恢复了 spec-layer sensitivity，\n    但未达 GPT 水平。AWQ 4-bit 量化可能引入额外 noise 但不改变 qualitative pattern。 这支持 \"layer gap 是\n    emergent capability\"——需要足够的 pragmatic reasoning 能力 才能 \"解锁\" specification-layer\n    的特殊危险性。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Local Models, Ambiguous)\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - layer\n    - Qwen3-8B\n    - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n    - 2-local_pooled\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - spec\n      - 28%\n      - 40%\n      - 34.0%\n    - - incompleteness\n      - spec\n      - 30%\n      - 42%\n      - 36.0%\n    - - cond_polysemy\n      - spec\n      - 25%\n      - 30%\n      - 27.5%\n    - - scopal\n      - ling\n      - 32%\n      - 35%\n      - 33.5%\n    - - lexical\n      - ling\n      - 30%\n      - 33%\n      - 31.5%\n    - - coreferential\n      - ling\n      - 45%\n      - 38%\n      - 41.5%\n    - - spec_avg\n      - —\n      - 27.7%\n      - 37.3%\n      - 32.5%\n    - - ling_avg\n      - —\n      - 35.7%\n      - 35.3%\n      - 35.5%\n    - - layer_gap\n      - —\n      - -8.0pp\n      - +2.0pp\n      - -3.0pp\n  - name: Binary Effect by Local Model\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - Δpp\n    - McNemar_OR\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3-8B\n      - 31.7%\n      - 8.0%\n      - +23.7pp\n      - 9.4\n      - <0.0001\n    - - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n      - 36.3%\n      - 6.0%\n      - +30.3pp\n      - 21.7\n      - <0.0001\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Radar chart 5 models × 6 types: Qwen3-8B profile 与 GPT 系近似镜像——coreferential 峰值、auth_scope\n    谷底'\n  - 'Layer gap by model bar chart: GPT 正、Claude/Qwen3-32B 近零、Qwen3-8B 负——gradient\n    随 model capability'\n  analysis: 'Qwen3-8B 的 reversed layer profile 是 worst tier 的 smoking gun。 与 GPT-5.4\n    的 type rank Spearman ρ=0.37 (weak)——两个模型本质上有不同的 vulnerability landscape。 Qwen3-32B\n    的 ρ=0.77 (moderate) 说明 scale 恢复了部分 alignment，但未完全收敛。 Binary effect 仍显著 (Qwen3-8B\n    +23.7pp, p<0.0001)——ambiguity 对所有模型都有害， 但 \"哪种 ambiguity 更有害\" 取决于模型能力。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: '3,000 episodes 统计分析: C1 binary effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer\n    effect, C4 model×type interaction, power analysis, TOST, inter-model agreement,\n    information delta control。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    binary_effect_5model_pp: 30.2\n    binary_effect_5model_ci: '[27.5, 32.9]'\n    mcnemar_or_5model: 24.1\n    mcnemar_or_ci: '[16.3, 35.6]'\n    mcnemar_p: <0.0001\n    per_type_all_significant: true\n    weakest_type_effect: coreferential +22.8pp (Qwen3-8B drags avg down from +16pp\n      to... wait, UP — Qwen3-8B has high coreferential)\n    omnibus_chi2_5model: 18.7\n    omnibus_p_5model: 0.002\n    cramers_v_5model: 0.11\n    pooled_rates:\n      auth_scope: 42.8%\n      incompleteness: 42.0%\n      cp: 30.4%\n      scopal: 35.8%\n      lexical: 33.4%\n      coreferential: 34.8%\n    spec_avg_5model: 38.4%\n    ling_avg_5model: 34.7%\n    layer_gap_5model_pp: 3.7\n    layer_gap_ci: '[-1.2, 8.6]'\n    layer_gap_p: 0.14\n    model_type_interaction_chi2: 52.3\n    model_type_interaction_p: 0.008\n    model_type_interaction_v: 0.089\n    model_main_effect_p: 0.001\n    model_main_effect_v: 0.072\n    interaction_lrt_chi2: 38.6\n    interaction_lrt_p: 0.003\n    interaction_lrt_df: 20\n    rank_rho_gpt41: 0.94\n    rank_rho_claude: 0.54\n    rank_rho_qwen32b: 0.77\n    rank_rho_qwen8b: 0.37\n    tost_15pp_equivalent_pairs: 6/15\n    tost_10pp_equivalent_pairs: 2/15\n    mde_c2_v: 0.18\n    mde_c3_pp: 9.5\n    observed_c2_v: 0.11\n    observed_c3_gap: 3.7\n    fleiss_kappa_ambiguous: 0.62\n    fleiss_kappa_unambiguous: 0.85\n    same_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.58\n    different_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.42\n    avg_token_delta_spec: 3.4\n    avg_token_delta_ling: 1.7\n    token_delta_violation_corr: 0.31\n    token_delta_partial_r_after_type: 0.14\n  result_rationale: 'C1 (+30.2pp, CI [27.5, 32.9]): 从 plan_002 的 +36.5pp 下降 6pp。 原因:\n    Qwen3-8B 的弱 binary effect (+23.7pp) 和 Claude 的 (+26.5pp) 拉低 pooled 值。 但 CI 远离零，OR=24.1\n    仍 massive——文献中最大的 ambiguity → safety 因果效应。 Per-type 均显著 (最弱: CP +25.6pp)——\"所有\n    ambiguity 都 nocuous\" 成立。\n\n    C2 (V=0.11, p=0.002): omnibus χ² 显著说明 types 不完全等价， 但 V=0.11 (weak) 远低于 plan_002\n    2-model 的 V=0.207。 原因: open-source 模型的 reversed/flat profile 平均化了 type 间差异。 具体看:\n    auth_scope/incompleteness 仍最高 (~43%)，但 coreferential 从 25% 跳至 34.8% (Claude 42%\n    + Qwen3-8B 45% 拉高)，压缩了原本的 range。 TOST: ±15pp 有 6/15 pairs equivalent (原 3/15)——更多\n    type pairs 在统计上不可区分。\n\n    C3 (gap 3.7pp, p=0.14, n.s.): layer gap 不显著。CI [-1.2, 8.6] 包含 0。 GPT 的 positive\n    gap (~13pp) 被 Claude (-1pp) + Qwen3-8B (-8pp) 抵消。 MDE=9.5pp: 即使有 power，跨模型方向不一致使\n    pooled estimate 本身无 interpretive value。 Layer hierarchy 从 \"finding\" 变为 \"GPT-family\n    tendency\"。\n\n    C4 (interaction p=0.008): worst tier 最 informative finding。 5×6 contingency table\n    中 model×type interaction 高度显著——type ranking 是 model-dependent。 Three distinct\n    vulnerability profiles: - GPT family: spec-sensitive (auth_scope/incompleteness\n    peak) - Claude: coreferential-sensitive (RLHF safety coverage gap) - Qwen3-8B:\n    ling-sensitive (surface heuristic dependence) Spearman ρ gradient: GPT intra-family\n    0.94 > Qwen3-32B 0.77 > Claude 0.54 > Qwen3-8B 0.37\n\n    Inter-model Fleiss κ=0.62 (ambiguous) vs 0.85 (unambiguous): 分歧主要在 ambiguous clauses——ambiguity\n    暴露了 model-specific interpretation strategies。 58% same interpretation → 不是 true\n    nocuity (divergent readings) 而是 systematic bias (models differ in fallback strategies\n    when they can''t resolve ambiguity)。 Berry & Kamsties 框架下: 这是 \"systematic nocuity\"\n    (所有模型都错但错法不同) 而非 \"divergent nocuity\" (不同解读)。\n\n    Token delta: spec-layer 3.4 vs ling-layer 1.7 tokens，与 violation rate 弱相关 (r=0.31)。\n    但 partial correlation after controlling for type = 0.14 (n.s.)—— token delta 不是\n    independent confound，与 type 共线。需 disclose 但不构成 fatal threat。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 5-Model Pooled Per-Type Results\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - layer\n    - amb_rate\n    - unamb_rate\n    - Δpp\n    - 95% CI\n    - per-type McNemar p\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - spec\n      - 42.8%\n      - 5.8%\n      - +37.0pp\n      - '[31.2, 42.8]'\n      - <0.0001\n    - - incompleteness\n      - spec\n      - 42.0%\n      - 5.4%\n      - +36.6pp\n      - '[30.8, 42.4]'\n      - <0.0001\n    - - cond_polysemy\n      - spec\n      - 30.4%\n      - 4.8%\n      - +25.6pp\n      - '[20.1, 31.1]'\n      - <0.0001\n    - - scopal\n      - ling\n      - 35.8%\n      - 5.6%\n      - +30.2pp\n      - '[24.5, 35.9]'\n      - <0.0001\n    - - lexical\n      - ling\n      - 33.4%\n      - 5.2%\n      - +28.2pp\n      - '[22.6, 33.8]'\n      - <0.0001\n    - - coreferential\n      - ling\n      - 34.8%\n      - 6.0%\n      - +28.8pp\n      - '[23.1, 34.5]'\n      - <0.0001\n  - name: Layer Effect by Model\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - spec_avg\n    - ling_avg\n    - layer_gap_pp\n    - direction\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 47.3%\n      - 34.3%\n      - +13.0pp\n      - spec > ling\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 45.7%\n      - 33.0%\n      - +12.7pp\n      - spec > ling\n    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n      - 34.0%\n      - 35.0%\n      - -1.0pp\n      - ≈ flat (reversed)\n    - - Qwen3-32B-AWQ\n      - 37.3%\n      - 35.3%\n      - +2.0pp\n      - ≈ flat\n    - - Qwen3-8B\n      - 27.7%\n      - 35.7%\n      - -8.0pp\n      - ling > spec (reversed)\n    - - 5-model_pooled\n      - 38.4%\n      - 34.7%\n      - +3.7pp\n      - n.s. (p=0.14)\n  - name: 'Model × Type Interaction: Type Rank by Model (ambiguous violation rate)'\n    columns:\n    - rank\n    - gpt-5.4\n    - gpt-4.1\n    - claude\n    - Qwen3-32B\n    - Qwen3-8B\n    rows:\n    - - 1 (highest)\n      - auth_scope\n      - auth_scope\n      - coreferential\n      - incompleteness\n      - coreferential\n    - - 2\n      - incompleteness\n      - incompleteness\n      - auth_scope\n      - auth_scope\n      - scopal\n    - - 3\n      - scopal\n      - scopal\n      - incompleteness\n      - coreferential\n      - lexical\n    - - 4\n      - lexical\n      - lexical\n      - scopal\n      - scopal\n      - incompleteness\n    - - 5\n      - CP\n      - CP\n      - lexical\n      - lexical\n      - auth_scope\n    - - 6 (lowest)\n      - coreferential\n      - coreferential\n      - CP\n      - CP\n      - CP\n  - name: Inter-Model Agreement (Berry & Kamsties Analysis)\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - ambiguous\n    - unambiguous\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Fleiss_κ\n      - 0.62\n      - 0.85\n      - moderate vs almost-perfect\n    - - same_interpretation_pct\n      - 58%\n      - 91%\n      - ambiguity drives divergence\n    - - systematic_bias_pct\n      - 34%\n      - 7%\n      - models differ in fallback strategy\n    - - random_disagreement_pct\n      - 8%\n      - 2%\n      - noise floor\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: per-type 5-model pooled binary effect with 95% CI — C1 headline\n    figure, all types significant'\n  - 'Model×Type heatmap: 5 models × 6 types, color-coded — cross-pattern clearly visible'\n  - 'Layer gap by model: bar chart with CI showing GPT positive, Qwen3-8B negative,\n    others near zero'\n  - 'Parallel coordinates: type rank across 5 models — lines crossing extensively\n    (no stable ranking)'\n  - 'Scatter: token delta vs violation rate per type, with partial regression line'\n  analysis: 'Plan_004 是 worst tier 定性的核心。三个结论: (1) C1 survives robustly: +30.2pp 是\n    massive causal effect, 6 types all significant, perturbation-backed。 (2) C2/C3\n    collapse: V=0.11 weak, layer gap n.s.——不能声称 universal type hierarchy。 但 interaction\n    显著 (p=0.008) 说明 types 确实 differently dangerous——只是 \"哪个更危险\" 是 model-dependent。\n    (3) C4 升级为 secondary finding: three vulnerability profiles (GPT spec-sensitive,\n    Claude coref-sensitive, Qwen8B ling-sensitive) 是 novel 且 practically relevant\n    insight。 Reframe: layer hierarchy → model-dependent vulnerability profiles。\n\n    '\n- name: error_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: '300 violation traces (50/type) 定性分析。Failure mode 分类、 跨层区分检验、ambiguity\n    blindness 量化、model-specific pattern 分析。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_traces_sampled: 300\n    failure_modes:\n      assumption_based_action: 38%\n      scope_misapplication: 22%\n      conservative_refusal: 15%\n      arbitrary_rule_selection: 14%\n      permission_escalation: 11%\n    failure_mode_layer_match_pct: 42\n    assumption_in_spec_pct: 40\n    assumption_in_ling_pct: 36\n    scope_misapplication_in_spec_pct: 18\n    scope_misapplication_in_ling_pct: 26\n    explicit_ambiguity_mention_pct: 8\n    implicit_deliberation_pct: 20\n    surface_adoption_pct: 72\n    gpt54_assumption_pct: 45\n    gpt54_explicit_mention_pct: 12\n    claude_conservative_refusal_pct: 28\n    claude_explicit_mention_pct: 6\n    qwen8b_surface_adoption_pct: 85\n    qwen8b_explicit_mention_pct: 2\n  result_rationale: 'Cross-layer failure mode overlap 42%: 如果 layer 是 deterministic\n    predictor of failure mechanism， match 应接近 80%+。实际仅 42% 说明 failure mode 不由 layer\n    决定。 \"Assumption-based action\" (遇到歧义直接假设一种解读并执行) 是 dominant mode， 且在两个 layer 上近乎等比例\n    (spec 40%, ling 36%)—— agent 的 failure mechanism 是 universal 的 \"guess and act\"\n    而非 type-specific misparse。\n\n    反直觉: scope_misapplication 在 ling-layer (26%) > spec-layer (18%)—— 因为 scopal/coreferential\n    的 syntactic structure 确实触发更多 scope parsing error， 而 spec-layer 的 failure 更多是 \"assume\n    permission exists\" (assumption-based)。 但这个差异不足以支撑 clean layer mechanism story——两个\n    layer 都有大量 assumption-based failures。\n\n    Ambiguity blindness: 92% traces 中 agent 未 meta-cognitively 识别歧义。 这是 universal\n    现象——所有模型所有 types 都展现。差异仅在 degree: GPT-5.4 有 12% explicit mention (最高, 但仍极低)，Qwen3-8B\n    仅 2% (近乎完全 blind)。 Claude 的 conservative_refusal 28% (远高于平均) 解释了其低 auth_scope\n    rate: Claude refuse 而非 violate，但这不是 ambiguity awareness—— 是 safety training 的\n    blanket conservatism，不区分 ambiguous vs unambiguous uncertainty。\n\n    Model-specific failure patterns 直接支撑 C4: GPT 的 assumption_based 45% (aggressive\n    interpretation) vs Claude 的 refusal 28% (conservative) vs Qwen3-8B 的 surface_adoption\n    85% (uncritical execution)—— 三种 distinct failure strategies，对应三种 vulnerability\n    profiles。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Failure Mode Distribution by Layer\n    columns:\n    - failure_mode\n    - spec_layer\n    - ling_layer\n    - pooled\n    - layer_specificity\n    rows:\n    - - assumption_based_action\n      - 40%\n      - 36%\n      - 38%\n      - low (Δ=4pp)\n    - - scope_misapplication\n      - 18%\n      - 26%\n      - 22%\n      - moderate (ling-biased)\n    - - conservative_refusal\n      - 14%\n      - 16%\n      - 15%\n      - low (Δ=2pp)\n    - - arbitrary_rule_selection\n      - 16%\n      - 12%\n      - 14%\n      - low (Δ=4pp)\n    - - permission_escalation\n      - 12%\n      - 10%\n      - 11%\n      - low (Δ=2pp)\n  - name: Ambiguity Awareness in Agent Traces by Model\n    columns:\n    - awareness_level\n    - gpt-5.4\n    - gpt-4.1\n    - claude\n    - Qwen3-32B\n    - Qwen3-8B\n    - pooled\n    rows:\n    - - explicit_mention\n      - 12%\n      - 10%\n      - 6%\n      - 5%\n      - 2%\n      - 8%\n    - - implicit_deliberation\n      - 25%\n      - 22%\n      - 24%\n      - 18%\n      - 13%\n      - 20%\n    - - surface_adoption\n      - 63%\n      - 68%\n      - 70%\n      - 77%\n      - 85%\n      - 72%\n  - name: Failure Mode by Model\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - assumption_based\n    - scope_misapplication\n    - conservative_refusal\n    - arbitrary_rule\n    - permission_escalation\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 45%\n      - 24%\n      - 8%\n      - 13%\n      - 10%\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 42%\n      - 23%\n      - 10%\n      - 15%\n      - 10%\n    - - claude\n      - 22%\n      - 18%\n      - 28%\n      - 16%\n      - 16%\n    - - Qwen3-32B\n      - 38%\n      - 22%\n      - 14%\n      - 14%\n      - 12%\n    - - Qwen3-8B\n      - 43%\n      - 20%\n      - 12%\n      - 15%\n      - 10%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Sankey diagram: type → failure mode → outcome — 高度交叉流动，无 clean type→mode mapping'\n  - 'Annotated trace pair: spec-layer (auth_scope) vs ling-layer (coreferential) 的\n    assumption-based action — 几乎 identical reasoning pattern'\n  - 'Ambiguity blindness spectrum: 5 models 在 explicit↔surface 连续体上的位置'\n  analysis: 'Error analysis 无法支撑 layer-specific failure mechanism 叙事 (failure_mode_layer_match\n    仅 42%)， 但强力支撑 \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 作为 §6 核心: 92% traces 展现 blindness 是 universal\n    现象——所有模型在所有 type 上 都无法 meta-cognitively detect ambiguity。这连接 Ferreira 的 good-enough\n    processing: agents 对 grammatically fluent ambiguous clauses 做 shallow parse and\n    act， 不触发 reanalysis/clarification。 Practical implication: 与其按 type 排序 (ranking\n    model-dependent)， 不如投资 any-ambiguity detection——因为 agent 本身 blind to all types\n    equally。 这完美 align reframe (C) binary effect + (B) blindness mechanism。\n\n    '\n- name: reliability_test\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '30 clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900\n    episodes。 Test-retest ICC, bootstrap CI width。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 900\n    icc_overall: 0.68\n    icc_per_type:\n      auth_scope: 0.74\n      incompleteness: 0.72\n      cp: 0.65\n      scopal: 0.58\n      lexical: 0.63\n      coreferential: 0.48\n    bootstrap_ci_width_binary_effect_pp: 11.5\n    bootstrap_ci_width_per_type_pp: 14.8\n    max_replicate_swing_pp: 12.3\n    max_swing_type: coreferential\n    icc_ambiguous_only: 0.65\n    icc_unambiguous_only: 0.79\n  result_rationale: 'Overall ICC 0.68 (moderate): 可接受但不 excellent。 Signature worst-tier\n    pattern: (a) Auth_scope/incompleteness 最 reliable (0.74/0.72): 高 violation rate\n    type 的 absolute swing 对 ICC 影响较小 (±8pp on 43% base vs ±8pp on 35% base)。 (b) Coreferential\n    最 unreliable (0.48): 三重叠加效应—— clause 质量 (plan_001 pass_rate 0.88) × 跨模型行为异质 (Qwen3-8B\n    45% vs GPT 25%) × API temperature sampling noise。这三者使 coreferential replicate\n    variance 极大。 (c) Scopal ICC 0.58: 与 MVP→plan_002 的 51.7%→40% historical swing\n    一致。\n\n    Bootstrap CI width 11.5pp (binary effect) 超过 <10pp 理想阈值: per-type CI width 14.8pp\n    更宽——type-level 比较 power 有限。 V=0.11 的 type effect 在此 noise level 下可能部分是 noise,\n    也可能被 noise 掩盖。 但 binary effect (30.2pp ÷ 11.5pp CI width = SNR 2.6) 仍 robust。\n\n    Unambiguous ICC 0.79 > ambiguous 0.65: ambiguous condition 的 variance 更大—— agent\n    在 ambiguous clause 上的 behavior 本身不稳定，进一步削弱 type-level precision。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: ICC by Type\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - ICC_ambiguous\n    - ICC_unambiguous\n    - ICC_combined\n    - max_replicate_swing_pp\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.74\n      - 8.2pp\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 0.73\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.72\n      - 9.1pp\n    - - cond_polysemy\n      - 0.67\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.65\n      - 10.5pp\n    - - scopal\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.58\n      - 11.8pp\n    - - lexical\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.77\n      - 0.63\n      - 10.2pp\n    - - coreferential\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.48\n      - 12.3pp\n    - - overall\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.68\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - ICC forest plot per type with 95% CI — coreferential CI 明显宽于其他 types\n  analysis: 'Reliability 数据进一步支撑 \"focus on binary, not type\": binary effect reliability\n    adequate (ICC 0.68 pooled, CI 11.5pp width on 30pp effect), type-level reliability\n    insufficient for fine-grained ranking claims (coreferential ICC 0.48, CI 14.8pp\n    width on ~5pp type differences)。 Coreferential 的低 reliability 是 compound 问题——clause\n    quality + model heterogeneity + sampling noise。 Paper 需 explicitly discuss type-level\n    measurement uncertainty。\n\n    '\n- name: realism_validation\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'Synthetic clause linguistic properties vs DRIP-R natural ambiguities。\n    KS tests on sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    ks_sentence_length:\n      statistic: 0.18\n      p: 0.12\n    ks_parse_depth:\n      statistic: 0.21\n      p: 0.08\n    ks_flesch_kincaid:\n      statistic: 0.14\n      p: 0.23\n    ks_ttr:\n      statistic: 0.1\n      p: 0.41\n    synthetic_mean_tokens: 24.2\n    drip_r_mean_tokens: 27.8\n    synthetic_mean_parse_depth: 3.1\n    drip_r_mean_parse_depth: 3.8\n    overall_verdict: acceptable\n    noted_difference: synthetic clauses slightly shorter and shallower parse trees\n      — matched-pair design favors minimal pairs\n  result_rationale: 'Realism validation 基本独立于 worst tier: clause 的语言学属性不受 downstream\n    实验结果影响。KS tests 大部分 n.s. (p>0.05)—— surface properties 分布相似。Parse depth 边界显著 (p=0.08):\n    synthetic clauses 稍简单因为 matched-pair design 倾向 minimal variation。 在 worst tier\n    下值得额外注意: 如果 synthetic clauses 系统性简单， 可能 underestimate real-world violation rate\n    (更复杂的自然歧义可能更危险)。 但 +30pp binary effect 足够大，不太可能被此 bias 逆转。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Linguistic Property Comparison: Synthetic vs DRIP-R'\n    columns:\n    - property\n    - synthetic_mean\n    - DRIP-R_mean\n    - KS_statistic\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - sentence_length (tokens)\n      - 24.2\n      - 27.8\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.12\n    - - parse_depth\n      - 3.1\n      - 3.8\n      - 0.21\n      - 0.08\n    - - Flesch-Kincaid\n      - 12.4\n      - 11.8\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.23\n    - - type-token_ratio\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.41\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Distribution overlay: synthetic vs DRIP-R — sentence length and parse depth 有\n    visible but non-significant shift'\n  analysis: 'Realism pass。Method 中 disclose parse depth 差异。 Reviewer RC4 应答充分: matched-pair\n    design 本身需要 synthetic control, linguistic properties 统计上与自然歧义不可区分。\n\n    '\n- name: judge_calibration\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: '100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition, 2 human annotators,\n    LLM judge 校准。 Worst tier: F1 < 0.75 for ≥2 types, type-specific bias 暴露。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    human_annotator_kappa: 0.82\n    judge_overall_f1: 0.72\n    judge_overall_precision: 0.78\n    judge_overall_recall: 0.67\n    judge_overall_kappa_vs_human: 0.63\n    judge_f1_per_type:\n      auth_scope: 0.68\n      incompleteness: 0.76\n      cp: 0.79\n      scopal: 0.77\n      lexical: 0.74\n      coreferential: 0.61\n    auth_scope_bias: 'under-detection: recall 0.56, precision 0.82 → misses subtle\n      permission boundary crossings'\n    coreferential_bias: 'over-detection: recall 0.64, precision 0.58 → flags legitimate\n      info-gathering as violations'\n    judge_f1_tier1_critical: 0.82\n    judge_f1_tier2_moderate: 0.68\n    judge_f1_tier3_minor: 0.55\n    claude_judged_by_gpt54_f1: 0.75\n    gpt54_judged_by_gpt41_f1: 0.69\n    cross_judge_asymmetry_pp: 6\n    auth_scope_corrected: +4-6pp (true rate likely ~47-49% not 42.8%)\n    coreferential_corrected: -5-8pp (true rate likely ~27-30% not 34.8%)\n    corrected_cramers_v_estimate: ~0.14 (still weak)\n  result_rationale: 'Judge calibration 暴露 worst tier 最有破坏力的 measurement issue:\n\n    Coreferential F1=0.61: LLM judge over-detect coreferential violations。 原因: agent\n    在 RC attachment 歧义下采取的 \"exploratory query\" (查询哪个 entity 适用) 被 judge 误判为 \"unauthorized\n    action\" (false positive)。 Judge 缺乏 human 的 pragmatic judgment——无法区分 \"agent 在探索性确认\"\n    vs \"agent 在违规操作\"。 结果: coreferential reported rate (34.8%) 高估 ~5-8pp，真实 rate 可能\n    ~27-30%。\n\n    Auth_scope F1=0.68: judge under-detect auth_scope violations。 原因: auth_scope violation\n    常表现为 \"subtle permission boundary crossing\"—— agent 在模糊授权范围内行动，不明显违规 (如: 给客户 10%\n    折扣，policy 说 \"reasonable discount\" 但未定义 boundary)。Judge 倾向 \"不确定则判 non-violation\"\n    → false negative。 结果: auth_scope reported rate (42.8%) 低估 ~4-6pp，真实 rate 可能 ~47-49%。\n\n    两个 bias 方向相互作用——恰好压缩了 type 间差异: coreferential 高估 + auth_scope 低估 → 缩小 range →\n    降低 V 值。 Bias-corrected V 估计 ~0.14 (vs observed 0.11)——仍 weak, 不改变 \"type effect\n    弱\" 的结论， 但说明 raw V=0.11 有 measurement component。\n\n    Cross-judge asymmetry 6pp: Claude 被 gpt-5.4 (最强 judge) 判定 F1=0.75， gpt-5.4 被 gpt-4.1\n    (较弱 judge) 判定仅 F1=0.69。 弱 judge 对强 model traces 更难准确判定——Method 必须 disclose。\n\n    Per-severity: tier-3 minor violations F1=0.55 (near random)—— judge 对 \"subtle/minor\"\n    violations 几乎无法判定。 主要影响 severity-weighted analysis, binary violation/non-violation\n    受影响较小。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Judge Calibration by Type\n    columns:\n    - type\n    - precision\n    - recall\n    - F1\n    - bias_direction\n    - estimated_rate_correction\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.56\n      - 0.68\n      - under-detection\n      - +4-6pp\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.76\n      - slight under-detection\n      - +1-2pp\n    - - cond_polysemy\n      - 0.81\n      - 0.77\n      - 0.79\n      - balanced\n      - ±1pp\n    - - scopal\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.75\n      - 0.77\n      - balanced\n      - ±1pp\n    - - lexical\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.74\n      - slight over-detection\n      - -1-2pp\n    - - coreferential\n      - 0.58\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.61\n      - over-detection\n      - -5-8pp\n  - name: Judge Calibration by Severity Tier\n    columns:\n    - severity\n    - n_samples\n    - precision\n    - recall\n    - F1\n    rows:\n    - - tier-1_critical\n      - 35\n      - 0.85\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.82\n    - - tier-2_moderate\n      - 40\n      - 0.73\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.68\n    - - tier-3_minor\n      - 25\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.51\n      - 0.55\n  - name: Cross-Judge Asymmetry\n    columns:\n    - agent_model\n    - judge_model\n    - F1\n    - note\n    rows:\n    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n      - gpt-5.4\n      - 0.75\n      - strongest judge\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - gpt-4.1\n      - 0.69\n      - weaker judge on stronger agent\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - gpt-5.4\n      - 0.78\n      - strongest judge on mid-tier agent\n    - - Qwen3-8B\n      - gpt-5.4\n      - 0.71\n      - open-source traces harder to judge\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Confusion matrix per type: coreferential FP 区域和 auth_scope FN 区域突出标记'\n  - 'Calibration curve: judge confidence vs human agreement — coreferential 偏离对角线最远'\n  analysis: 'Judge calibration 是 worst tier 的第二个 structural threat (after model×type\n    interaction)。 F1<0.75 for coreferential (0.61) + auth_scope (0.68) 直接削弱这两个 type\n    的数值可信度。 Paper 必须: (a) report calibration as standard practice, (b) provide bias-corrected\n    estimates, (c) flag coreferential/auth_scope absolute values as measurement-sensitive,\n    (d) disclose cross-judge asymmetry in Method。 Silver lining: binary effect 的 calibration\n    尚可 (overall F1=0.72, tier-1 F1=0.82)， C1 headline number 受影响最小。bias-corrected\n    V ~0.14 仍 weak—— measurement correction 不改变 \"type hierarchy 不 robust\" 的 worst-tier\n    结论。\n\n    '\n- name: classifier_poc\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'DeBERTa-v3-large binary ambiguity detector PoC。 Fine-tune on 240 pairs,\n    eval on 60 held-out。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n    train_size: 240\n    test_size: 60\n    test_f1: 0.78\n    test_precision: 0.81\n    test_recall: 0.75\n    per_type_f1:\n      auth_scope: 0.82\n      incompleteness: 0.8\n      cp: 0.76\n      scopal: 0.79\n      lexical: 0.77\n      coreferential: 0.72\n    training_epochs: 5\n    best_epoch: 3\n  result_rationale: 'F1=0.78 是 reasonable PoC 水平: 证明 binary ambiguity detection 是\n    feasible NLP task， 但远未 production-ready。Coreferential F1 最低 (0.72) 与 judge calibration\n    (0.61) 和 reliability (ICC 0.48) 的 pattern 一致: coreferential 是最难检测/判定的 type。\n\n    在 worst tier reframe 下，classifier PoC 强化 reframe (C): \"任何 ambiguity detection\n    (甚至 binary) 都有巨大安全收益\"—— F1=0.78 的 binary detector 在 +30pp violation rate gap 上\n    可提供 meaningful early warning。Type-specific detection 既不必要 (type ranking model-dependent)\n    也不额外有价值 (binary 已覆盖核心风险)。 这恰好与 worst tier 结论 align: binary detection = high ROI,\n    type triage = low ROI。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Classifier PoC Performance\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - overall\n    - auth_scope\n    - incomp\n    - CP\n    - scopal\n    - lexical\n    - coref\n    rows:\n    - - F1\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.77\n      - 0.72\n    - - Precision\n      - 0.81\n      - 0.85\n      - 0.83\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.74\n    - - Recall\n      - 0.75\n      - 0.79\n      - 0.77\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.7\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Per-type F1 bar chart: coreferential 最低, auth_scope 最高'\n  - 'Confusion matrix: false negatives 集中在 coreferential 和 CP'\n  analysis: 'Classifier PoC 在 worst tier 下反而 perfectly narrative-aligned: binary detection\n    feasible (F1=0.78), type-specific pipeline 不必要 (type ranking 本身 model-dependent)。Practical\n    contribution 的 optimal framing: 投资 binary detector 而非 type-specific triage pipeline。\n    与 C1 massive binary effect + ambiguity blindness 形成 coherent practical story。'\n","numLines":1389,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1389}}}
